window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b097-8b49ce4f1e4834aa.json"]={sha256:"8b49ce4f1e4834aa9379bde525ea10d2821cf211d1b5c89b141091b07976adb8",value:{"id":"b097","title":"施工測量控制網","titleEn":"Construction surveying control networks","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從控制網層級與精度預算出發，說明投影比例因子、觀測墩與強制對心、全測站與 GNSS 的精度規格與 ISO 17123 現場檢定，再處理導線與最小二乘平差、高層建築軸線垂直傳遞、GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算、長隧道貫通誤差，以及控制網複測、參考框架與交接紀錄，並以戈達基線隧道、英法海底隧道與 Crossrail 的公開資料對照。","summaryEn":"Starting from network hierarchy and accuracy budgets, explain projection scale factors, pillars and forced centring, total-station and GNSS specifications with ISO 17123 field tests, then traverses and least-squares adjustment, vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings, static GNSS and height conversion, long-tunnel breakthrough error, and finally network re-survey, reference frames and handover records, compared with public data from the Gotthard Base Tunnel, the Channel Tunnel and Crossrail.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-facade-digital","subcategoryTitle":"帷幕牆、垂直運輸與數位營建","subcategoryTitleEn":"Facades, vertical transport and digital construction","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-facade-digital","learningTags":["structures","st-facade-digital","survey"],"architectureFamily":"survey","architectureNodes":[["國家坐標框架","National reference frame"],["GNSS 主控制網","GNSS primary network"],["導線加密與平差","Traverse densification and adjustment"],["放樣與垂直傳遞","Set-out and vertical transfer"],["複測與穩定性檢定","Re-survey and stability testing"],["控制成果紀錄與交接","Control records and handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[4,1],[4,3],[1,5],[4,5]],"diagram":{"type":"survey","labels":["國家坐標框架","GNSS 主控制網","導線加密與平差","放樣與垂直傳遞","複測與穩定性檢定"],"labelsEn":["National reference frame","GNSS primary network","Traverse densification and adjustment","Set-out and vertical transfer","Re-survey and stability testing"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：以極座標法從控制觀測墩放樣錨栓，控制點本身標準差 2.0 mm，全測站測距 ±(1 mm + 1 ppm)、測角 1″（4.85×10⁻⁶ rad），放樣公差 ±10 mm（95%）。距離 D = 150 m 時，測距 σ_D = 1 + 0.15 = 1.15 mm，橫向 D·σ_θ = 150×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.73 mm，合成 σ = √(1.15² + 0.73² + 2.0²) = √5.85 ≈ 2.42 mm，95% 約 1.96×2.42 ≈ 4.7 mm，合格。D = 400 m 時 σ_D = 1.4 mm、橫向 1.94 mm，σ = √9.72 ≈ 3.12 mm，95% 約 6.1 mm，仍合格但餘裕變小，宜改由較近的控制點放樣。若忘記套用 148 ppm 的合併比例因子，400 m 的距離就多出 400×148×10⁻⁶ ≈ 59 mm 的系統誤差，遠大於所有隨機誤差的總和。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際專案。","textEn":"Design exercise: anchor bolts are set out by polar method from a control pillar whose own standard deviation is 2.0 mm, using a total station with ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) distance and 1″ (4.85×10⁻⁶ rad) angle accuracy, against a set-out tolerance of ±10 mm at 95%. At D = 150 m the distance term is σ_D = 1 + 0.15 = 1.15 mm and the lateral term D·σ_θ = 150×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.73 mm, giving σ = √(1.15² + 0.73² + 2.0²) = √5.85 ≈ 2.42 mm and a 95% value of about 1.96×2.42 ≈ 4.7 mm, which passes. At D = 400 m, σ_D = 1.4 mm and the lateral term is 1.94 mm, so σ = √9.72 ≈ 3.12 mm and the 95% value is about 6.1 mm, still passing but with less margin, so a closer control point is preferable. Forgetting the 148 ppm combined scale factor adds a systematic error of 400×148×10⁻⁶ ≈ 59 mm at 400 m, far more than all the random errors together. Values are teaching assumptions, not any real project.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b097-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網層級與精度預算」與「坐標系統、格網與地面比例」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget\" and \"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b097-v13-01","title":"控制網層級與精度預算：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「主控制網」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Primary control network” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"施工測量的原則是先整體、後局部，先控制、後碎部：國家坐標框架提供絕對位置，專案主控制網以 GNSS 與精密全測站建立少數高精度點，再以導線加密成次級控制，最後才由工作點放樣柱位、錨栓與模板。每一層的誤差都會傳到下一層，所以控制網不是測得越多越好，而是先從結構允許的放樣公差倒推每一層可分配的誤差，再選擇儀器、網形與觀測次數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「主控制網」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Construction surveying works from the whole to the part and from control to detail: the national frame gives absolute position, the project's primary network establishes a few high-accuracy points by GNSS and precise total station, traverses densify it into secondary control, and only then do working points set out columns, anchor bolts and formwork. Errors at each level pass to the next, so a control network is not about measuring as much as possible but about working back from the structure's set-out tolerance to the error each level may consume, then choosing instruments, geometry and number of observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Primary control network” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：放樣公差 ±10 mm（95%）對應總標準差 σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A set-out tolerance of ±10 mm at 95% means a total standard deviation σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「主控制網」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Primary control network”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-01-k1","title":"控制網層級與精度預算","titleEn":"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget","text":"施工測量的原則是先整體、後局部，先控制、後碎部：國家坐標框架提供絕對位置，專案主控制網以 GNSS 與精密全測站建立少數高精度點，再以導線加密成次級控制，最後才由工作點放樣柱位、錨栓與模板。每一層的誤差都會傳到下一層，所以控制網不是測得越多越好，而是先從結構允許的放樣公差倒推每一層可分配的誤差，再選擇儀器、網形與觀測次數。","textEn":"Construction surveying works from the whole to the part and from control to detail: the national frame gives absolute position, the project's primary network establishes a few high-accuracy points by GNSS and precise total station, traverses densify it into secondary control, and only then do working points set out columns, anchor bolts and formwork. Errors at each level pass to the next, so a control network is not about measuring as much as possible but about working back from the structure's set-out tolerance to the error each level may consume, then choosing instruments, geometry and number of observations.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網層級與精度預算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget\" is correct?","options":["只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。","施工測量的原則是先整體、後局部，先控制、後碎部：國家坐標框架提供絕對位置，專案主控制網以 GNSS 與精密全測站建立少數高精度點，再以導線加密成次級控制，最後才由工作點放樣柱位、錨栓與模板。","坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。"],"optionsEn":["With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation.","Construction surveying works from the whole to the part and from control to detail: the national frame gives absolute position, the project's primary network establishes a few high-accuracy points by GNSS and precise total station, traverses densify it into secondary control, and only then do working points set out columns, anchor bolts and formwork.","The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground."],"answer":1,"explanation":"施工測量的原則是先整體、後局部，先控制、後碎部：國家坐標框架提供絕對位置，專案主控制網以 GNSS 與精密全測站建立少數高精度點，再以導線加密成次級控制，最後才由工作點放樣柱位、錨栓與模板。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Construction surveying works from the whole to the part and from control to detail: the national frame gives absolute position, the project's primary network establishes a few high-accuracy points by GNSS and precise total station, traverses densify it into secondary control, and only then do working points set out columns, anchor bolts and formwork. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b097-v13-02","title":"控制網層級與精度預算：定量估算","titleEn":"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「主控制網」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Primary control network” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：放樣公差 ±10 mm（95%）對應總標準差 σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm。主控制網分配 σ_p = 2 mm、次級控制 σ_s = 3 mm，放樣作業可用 σ_o = √(5.1² − 2² − 3²) = √(26.0 − 4 − 9) = √13.0 ≈ 3.6 mm。若主控制只達 4 mm，σ_o = √(26.0 − 16 − 9) = 1.0 mm，現場幾乎無法達成。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A set-out tolerance of ±10 mm at 95% means a total standard deviation σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm. Allocating σ_p = 2 mm to primary control and σ_s = 3 mm to secondary control leaves σ_o = √(5.1² − 2² − 3²) = √(26.0 − 4 − 9) = √13.0 ≈ 3.6 mm for set-out. If primary control only reaches 4 mm, σ_o = √(26.0 − 16 − 9) = 1.0 mm, which is barely achievable on site. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在測量計畫中列出每一層控制的精度目標與驗證方式：主控制網以最小二乘平差的誤差橢圓、次級導線以閉合差、放樣點以獨立檢核（由另一控制點或另一組人員重測）確認；三者合成後與結構及帷幕牆的公差規定比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The survey plan lists the accuracy target and check method for each level: error ellipses from the least-squares adjustment for primary control, misclosures for secondary traverses and independent checks for set-out points (re-measured from another control point or by another crew); the combined result is compared with the structural and façade tolerance requirements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"放樣公差 ±10 mm（95%）對應總標準差 σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm。主控制網分配 σ_p = 2 mm、次級控制 σ_s = 3 mm，放樣作業可用 σ_o = √(5.1² − 2² − 3²) = √(26.0 − 4 − 9) = √13.0 ≈ 3.6 mm。若主控制只達 4 mm，σ_o = √(26.0 − 16 − 9) = 1.0 mm，現場幾乎無法達成。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A set-out tolerance of ±10 mm at 95% means a total standard deviation σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm. Allocating σ_p = 2 mm to primary control and σ_s = 3 mm to secondary control leaves σ_o = √(5.1² − 2² − 3²) = √(26.0 − 4 − 9) = √13.0 ≈ 3.6 mm for set-out. If primary control only reaches 4 mm, σ_o = √(26.0 − 16 − 9) = 1.0 mm, which is barely achievable on site. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網層級與精度預算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget\", which statement holds?","options":["儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。","超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。","放樣公差 ±10 mm（95%）對應總標準差 σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm。"],"optionsEn":["The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site.","A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment.","A set-out tolerance of ±10 mm at 95% means a total standard deviation σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"放樣公差 ±10 mm（95%）對應總標準差 σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A set-out tolerance of ±10 mm at 95% means a total standard deviation σ = 10/1.96 ≈ 5.1 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b097-v13-03","title":"控制網層級與精度預算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「主控制網」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Primary control network” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在測量計畫中列出每一層控制的精度目標與驗證方式：主控制網以最小二乘平差的誤差橢圓、次級導線以閉合差、放樣點以獨立檢核（由另一控制點或另一組人員重測）確認；三者合成後與結構及帷幕牆的公差規定比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The survey plan lists the accuracy target and check method for each level: error ellipses from the least-squares adjustment for primary control, misclosures for secondary traverses and independent checks for set-out points (re-measured from another control point or by another crew); the combined result is compared with the structural and façade tolerance requirements. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：開工前提交測量計畫，列出控制點分布、儀器、觀測方法、精度目標與檢核頻率，交由業主的測量顧問審查；每一個放樣成果都必須有獨立檢核紀錄才可交付下一工序。","observationEn":"Site practice: Before work starts submit a survey plan listing control-point layout, instruments, observation methods, accuracy targets and check frequency for review by the owner's survey consultant; every set-out result needs an independent check record before it is handed to the next trade.","failure":"注意干擾：承包商只用一個控制點以單一極座標法放樣整個基地，沒有任何獨立檢核；控制點被機具撞動數公分後，整排錨栓隨之偏移，直到鋼柱吊裝時才發現對不上。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A contractor sets out the whole site by polar method from a single control point without any independent check; when plant knocks the point by a few centimetres the whole row of anchor bolts shifts with it, and the error is found only when steel columns will not fit at erection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在測量計畫中列出每一層控制的精度目標與驗證方式：主控制網以最小二乘平差的誤差橢圓、次級導線以閉合差、放樣點以獨立檢核（由另一控制點或另一組人員重測）確認；三者合成後與結構及帷幕牆的公差規定比較。","textEn":"The survey plan lists the accuracy target and check method for each level: error ellipses from the least-squares adjustment for primary control, misclosures for secondary traverses and independent checks for set-out points (re-measured from another control point or by another crew); the combined result is compared with the structural and façade tolerance requirements.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"開工前提交測量計畫，列出控制點分布、儀器、觀測方法、精度目標與檢核頻率，交由業主的測量顧問審查；每一個放樣成果都必須有獨立檢核紀錄才可交付下一工序。","textEn":"Before work starts submit a survey plan listing control-point layout, instruments, observation methods, accuracy targets and check frequency for review by the owner's survey consultant; every set-out result needs an independent check record before it is handed to the next trade.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網層級與精度預算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget\"?","options":["在測量計畫中列出每一層控制的精度目標與驗證方式：主控制網以最小二乘平差的誤差橢圓、次級導線以閉合差、放樣點以獨立檢核（由另一控制點或另一組人員重測）確認。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。"],"optionsEn":["The survey plan lists the accuracy target and check method for each level: error ellipses from the least-squares adjustment for primary control, misclosures for secondary traverses and independent checks for set-out points (re-measured from another control point or by another crew).","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在測量計畫中列出每一層控制的精度目標與驗證方式：主控制網以最小二乘平差的誤差橢圓、次級導線以閉合差、放樣點以獨立檢核（由另一控制點或另一組人員重測）確認；三者合成後與結構及帷幕牆的公差規定比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The survey plan lists the accuracy target and check method for each level: error ellipses from the least-squares adjustment for primary control, misclosures for secondary traverses and independent checks for set-out points (re-measured from another control point or by another crew); the combined result is compared with the structural and façade tolerance requirements. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b097-v13-04","title":"控制網層級與精度預算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「主控制網」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Primary control network” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"承包商只用一個控制點以單一極座標法放樣整個基地，沒有任何獨立檢核；控制點被機具撞動數公分後，整排錨栓隨之偏移，直到鋼柱吊裝時才發現對不上。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A contractor sets out the whole site by polar method from a single control point without any independent check; when plant knocks the point by a few centimetres the whole row of anchor bolts shifts with it, and the error is found only when steel columns will not fit at erection. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：每一層的誤差都會傳到下一層，所以控制網不是測得越多越好，而是先從結構允許的放樣公差倒推每一層可分配的誤差，再選擇儀器、網形與觀測次數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Errors at each level pass to the next, so a control network is not about measuring as much as possible but about working back from the structure's set-out tolerance to the error each level may consume, then choosing instruments, geometry and number of observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"承包商只用一個控制點以單一極座標法放樣整個基地，沒有任何獨立檢核；控制點被機具撞動數公分後，整排錨栓隨之偏移，直到鋼柱吊裝時才發現對不上。","textEn":"A contractor sets out the whole site by polar method from a single control point without any independent check; when plant knocks the point by a few centimetres the whole row of anchor bolts shifts with it, and the error is found only when steel columns will not fit at erection.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網層級與精度預算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control-network hierarchy and accuracy budget\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","承包商只用一個控制點以單一極座標法放樣整個基地，沒有任何獨立檢核；控制點被機具撞動數公分後，整排錨栓隨之偏移，直到鋼柱吊裝時才發現對不上。","坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A contractor sets out the whole site by polar method from a single control point without any independent check.","The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground."],"answer":1,"explanation":"承包商只用一個控制點以單一極座標法放樣整個基地，沒有任何獨立檢核；控制點被機具撞動數公分後，整排錨栓隨之偏移，直到鋼柱吊裝時才發現對不上。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A contractor sets out the whole site by polar method from a single control point without any independent check; when plant knocks the point by a few centimetres the whole row of anchor bolts shifts with it, and the error is found only when steel columns will not fit at erection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b097-v13-05","title":"坐標系統、格網與地面比例：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「合併比例因子」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Combined scale factor” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"坐標格網是把地球曲面投影到平面的結果，格網距離與地面實際距離之間有比例差：橫麥卡托投影在中央經線處比例因子小於 1，離中央經線越遠越大；同時測站越高，地面距離歸算到橢球面後越短。兩者相乘的合併比例因子在長距離工程中可達每公里數十到上百公釐，因此長線形工程常建立低變形的專案坐標系，並在測量計畫中明定格網與地面距離的換算方式。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「合併比例因子」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A coordinate grid is a projection of the curved Earth onto a plane, so grid distances differ from ground distances by a scale: on a transverse Mercator projection the scale factor is below 1 at the central meridian and grows with distance from it, while the higher the site, the shorter a ground distance becomes when reduced to the ellipsoid. Their product, the combined scale factor, can amount to tens or hundreds of millimetres per kilometre on long works, so linear projects often set up low-distortion project coordinate systems and the survey plan states how grid and ground distances are converted. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Combined scale factor” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：台灣 TM2 投影中央經線 121°E、k₀ = 0.9999。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Taiwan's TM2 projection has central meridian 121°E and k₀ = 0.9999.","failure":"常見誤解：「坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「合併比例因子」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Combined scale factor”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-05-k1","title":"坐標系統、格網與地面比例","titleEn":"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale","text":"坐標格網是把地球曲面投影到平面的結果，格網距離與地面實際距離之間有比例差：橫麥卡托投影在中央經線處比例因子小於 1，離中央經線越遠越大；同時測站越高，地面距離歸算到橢球面後越短。兩者相乘的合併比例因子在長距離工程中可達每公里數十到上百公釐，因此長線形工程常建立低變形的專案坐標系，並在測量計畫中明定格網與地面距離的換算方式。","textEn":"A coordinate grid is a projection of the curved Earth onto a plane, so grid distances differ from ground distances by a scale: on a transverse Mercator projection the scale factor is below 1 at the central meridian and grows with distance from it, while the higher the site, the shorter a ground distance becomes when reduced to the ellipsoid. Their product, the combined scale factor, can amount to tens or hundreds of millimetres per kilometre on long works, so linear projects often set up low-distortion project coordinate systems and the survey plan states how grid and ground distances are converted.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「坐標系統、格網與地面比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale\" is correct?","options":["坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。","控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。","坐標格網是把地球曲面投影到平面的結果，格網距離與地面實際距離之間有比例差：橫麥卡托投影在中央經線處比例因子小於 1，離中央經線越遠越大。"],"optionsEn":["The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground.","Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change.","A coordinate grid is a projection of the curved Earth onto a plane, so grid distances differ from ground distances by a scale: on a transverse Mercator projection the scale factor is below 1 at the central meridian and grows with distance from it, while the higher the site, the shorter a ground distance becomes when reduced to the ellipsoid."],"answer":2,"explanation":"坐標格網是把地球曲面投影到平面的結果，格網距離與地面實際距離之間有比例差：橫麥卡托投影在中央經線處比例因子小於 1，離中央經線越遠越大；同時測站越高，地面距離歸算到橢球面後越短。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A coordinate grid is a projection of the curved Earth onto a plane, so grid distances differ from ground distances by a scale: on a transverse Mercator projection the scale factor is below 1 at the central meridian and grows with distance from it, while the higher the site, the shorter a ground distance becomes when reduced to the ellipsoid. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b097-v13-06","title":"坐標系統、格網與地面比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「合併比例因子」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Combined scale factor” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：台灣 TM2 投影中央經線 121°E、k₀ = 0.9999。距中央經線 50 km：k ≈ 0.9999×(1 + 50,000²/(2×6,371,000²)) ≈ 0.9999×1.0000308 ≈ 0.99993；高程 500 m 的高程因子 6,371,000/6,371,500 ≈ 0.999922。合併因子 ≈ 0.99993×0.999922 ≈ 0.999852，地面 1,000 m 對應格網 999.852 m，差約 148 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Taiwan's TM2 projection has central meridian 121°E and k₀ = 0.9999. At 50 km from the meridian k ≈ 0.9999×(1 + 50,000²/(2×6,371,000²)) ≈ 0.9999×1.0000308 ≈ 0.99993; at 500 m elevation the height factor is 6,371,000/6,371,500 ≈ 0.999922. The combined factor ≈ 0.99993×0.999922 ≈ 0.999852, so 1,000 m on the ground is 999.852 m on the grid, about 148 mm less. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在基地兩端的控制點之間以全測站直接量測地面距離，與由坐標反算的格網距離比較，差值應符合計算的合併比例因子；設計、測量與鋼構製造廠須確認使用同一套距離換算，並在圖說上標示坐標系統與比例處理方式。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the ground distance between control points at the two ends of the site directly with a total station and compare it with the grid distance computed from coordinates; the difference should match the computed combined scale factor.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"台灣 TM2 投影中央經線 121°E、k₀ = 0.9999。距中央經線 50 km：k ≈ 0.9999×(1 + 50,000²/(2×6,371,000²)) ≈ 0.9999×1.0000308 ≈ 0.99993；高程 500 m 的高程因子 6,371,000/6,371,500 ≈ 0.999922。合併因子 ≈ 0.99993×0.999922 ≈ 0.999852，地面 1,000 m 對應格網 999.852 m，差約 148 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Taiwan's TM2 projection has central meridian 121°E and k₀ = 0.9999. At 50 km from the meridian k ≈ 0.9999×(1 + 50,000²/(2×6,371,000²)) ≈ 0.9999×1.0000308 ≈ 0.99993; at 500 m elevation the height factor is 6,371,000/6,371,500 ≈ 0.999922. The combined factor ≈ 0.99993×0.999922 ≈ 0.999852, so 1,000 m on the ground is 999.852 m on the grid, about 148 mm less. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「坐標系統、格網與地面比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale\", which statement holds?","options":["台灣 TM2 投影中央經線 121°E、k₀ = 0.9999。","閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。","GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。"],"optionsEn":["Taiwan's TM2 projection has central meridian 121°E and k₀ = 0.9999.","A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors.","The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"台灣 TM2 投影中央經線 121°E、k₀ = 0.9999。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Taiwan's TM2 projection has central meridian 121°E and k₀ = 0.9999. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b097-v13-07","title":"坐標系統、格網與地面比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「合併比例因子」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Combined scale factor” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在基地兩端的控制點之間以全測站直接量測地面距離，與由坐標反算的格網距離比較，差值應符合計算的合併比例因子；設計、測量與鋼構製造廠須確認使用同一套距離換算，並在圖說上標示坐標系統與比例處理方式。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the ground distance between control points at the two ends of the site directly with a total station and compare it with the grid distance computed from coordinates; the difference should match the computed combined scale factor. Designers, surveyors and the steel fabricator must confirm they use the same distance conversion, and drawings must state the coordinate system and how scale is handled. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：測量計畫要明定坐標系統、投影、高程基準與合併比例因子，長線形工程應評估是否採用低變形專案坐標；製造圖尺寸一律以地面尺寸標註，換算方法由測量主管簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The survey plan must define the coordinate system, projection, height datum and combined scale factor, and for long linear works assess a low-distortion project grid; fabrication-drawing dimensions are always given as ground dimensions, with the conversion method signed off by the survey lead.","failure":"注意干擾：設計以格網坐標出圖，鋼構廠卻依圖上尺寸以地面長度製造，在長約 1 km 的高架或長廊上累積出十幾公分的長度差，最後幾跨的梁與支承對不上，只能現場切割或重新製造。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Design issues drawings in grid coordinates while the steel fabricator builds to ground lengths from the dimensions, so over a viaduct or concourse about 1 km long the length difference accumulates to more than 100 mm and the last spans' girders do not meet their bearings, forcing site cutting or refabrication. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在基地兩端的控制點之間以全測站直接量測地面距離，與由坐標反算的格網距離比較，差值應符合計算的合併比例因子；設計、測量與鋼構製造廠須確認使用同一套距離換算，並在圖說上標示坐標系統與比例處理方式。","textEn":"Measure the ground distance between control points at the two ends of the site directly with a total station and compare it with the grid distance computed from coordinates; the difference should match the computed combined scale factor. Designers, surveyors and the steel fabricator must confirm they use the same distance conversion, and drawings must state the coordinate system and how scale is handled.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"測量計畫要明定坐標系統、投影、高程基準與合併比例因子，長線形工程應評估是否採用低變形專案坐標；製造圖尺寸一律以地面尺寸標註，換算方法由測量主管簽認。","textEn":"The survey plan must define the coordinate system, projection, height datum and combined scale factor, and for long linear works assess a low-distortion project grid; fabrication-drawing dimensions are always given as ground dimensions, with the conversion method signed off by the survey lead.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「坐標系統、格網與地面比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在基地兩端的控制點之間以全測站直接量測地面距離，與由坐標反算的格網距離比較，差值應符合計算的合併比例因子。","監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Measure the ground distance between control points at the two ends of the site directly with a total station and compare it with the grid distance computed from coordinates.","Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在基地兩端的控制點之間以全測站直接量測地面距離，與由坐標反算的格網距離比較，差值應符合計算的合併比例因子；設計、測量與鋼構製造廠須確認使用同一套距離換算，並在圖說上標示坐標系統與比例處理方式。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the ground distance between control points at the two ends of the site directly with a total station and compare it with the grid distance computed from coordinates; the difference should match the computed combined scale factor. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b097-v13-08","title":"坐標系統、格網與地面比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「合併比例因子」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Combined scale factor” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"設計以格網坐標出圖，鋼構廠卻依圖上尺寸以地面長度製造，在長約 1 km 的高架或長廊上累積出十幾公分的長度差，最後幾跨的梁與支承對不上，只能現場切割或重新製造。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Design issues drawings in grid coordinates while the steel fabricator builds to ground lengths from the dimensions, so over a viaduct or concourse about 1 km long the length difference accumulates to more than 100 mm and the last spans' girders do not meet their bearings, forcing site cutting or refabrication. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：兩者相乘的合併比例因子在長距離工程中可達每公里數十到上百公釐，因此長線形工程常建立低變形的專案坐標系，並在測量計畫中明定格網與地面距離的換算方式。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Their product, the combined scale factor, can amount to tens or hundreds of millimetres per kilometre on long works, so linear projects often set up low-distortion project coordinate systems and the survey plan states how grid and ground distances are converted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"設計以格網坐標出圖，鋼構廠卻依圖上尺寸以地面長度製造，在長約 1 km 的高架或長廊上累積出十幾公分的長度差，最後幾跨的梁與支承對不上，只能現場切割或重新製造。","textEn":"Design issues drawings in grid coordinates while the steel fabricator builds to ground lengths from the dimensions, so over a viaduct or concourse about 1 km long the length difference accumulates to more than 100 mm and the last spans' girders do not meet their bearings, forcing site cutting or refabrication.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「坐標系統、格網與地面比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Coordinate systems, grid and ground scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。","設計以格網坐標出圖，鋼構廠卻依圖上尺寸以地面長度製造，在長約 1 km 的高架或長廊上累積出十幾公分的長度差，最後幾跨的梁與支承對不上，只能現場切割或重新製造。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change.","Design issues drawings in grid coordinates while the steel fabricator builds to ground lengths from the dimensions, so over a viaduct or concourse about 1 km long the length difference accumulates to more than 100 mm and the last spans' girders do not meet their bearings, forcing site cutting or refabrication."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設計以格網坐標出圖，鋼構廠卻依圖上尺寸以地面長度製造，在長約 1 km 的高架或長廊上累積出十幾公分的長度差，最後幾跨的梁與支承對不上，只能現場切割或重新製造。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Design issues drawings in grid coordinates while the steel fabricator builds to ground lengths from the dimensions, so over a viaduct or concourse about 1 km long the length difference accumulates to more than 100 mm and the last spans' girders do not meet their bearings, forcing site cutting or refabrication. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b097-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性」與「儀器精度規格與現場檢定」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Monuments, pillars and point stability\" and \"Instrument specifications and field testing\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b097-v13-09","title":"控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Monuments, pillars and point stability: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「強制對心觀測墩」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Forced-centring pillars” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"控制網的精度不只取決於儀器，也取決於控制點本身是否穩定。主控制點常做成深入穩定地層的混凝土觀測墩，頂部埋設強制對心盤，讓儀器與稜鏡每次都安裝在同一點，消除對心誤差；地面標石則要避開開挖影響範圍、施工便道與排水路徑。觀測墩本身也會受日照溫差與地下水變化而微小移動，所以重要工程會在影響範圍外另設參考點，用來判斷控制點是否移動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「強制對心觀測墩」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A network's accuracy depends not only on instruments but on whether the control points themselves are stable. Primary points are often concrete pillars founded in stable ground with forced-centring plates on top so that instrument and prism are mounted at exactly the same point every time, removing centring error; ground marks must avoid the zone of excavation influence, haul roads and drainage paths. Pillars also move slightly with solar heating and groundwater changes, so major works add reference points outside the zone of influence to judge whether control points have moved. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Forced-centring pillars” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：對心誤差造成的角度誤差 ε = e/D。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Angular error from centring ε = e/D.","failure":"常見誤解：「控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「強制對心觀測墩」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Forced-centring pillars”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-09-k1","title":"控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性","titleEn":"Monuments, pillars and point stability","text":"控制網的精度不只取決於儀器，也取決於控制點本身是否穩定。主控制點常做成深入穩定地層的混凝土觀測墩，頂部埋設強制對心盤，讓儀器與稜鏡每次都安裝在同一點，消除對心誤差；地面標石則要避開開挖影響範圍、施工便道與排水路徑。","textEn":"A network's accuracy depends not only on instruments but on whether the control points themselves are stable. Primary points are often concrete pillars founded in stable ground with forced-centring plates on top so that instrument and prism are mounted at exactly the same point every time, removing centring error; ground marks must avoid the zone of excavation influence, haul roads and drainage paths.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Monuments, pillars and point stability\" is correct?","options":["控制網的精度不只取決於儀器，也取決於控制點本身是否穩定。","控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。","儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。"],"optionsEn":["A network's accuracy depends not only on instruments but on whether the control points themselves are stable.","Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change.","The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site."],"answer":0,"explanation":"控制網的精度不只取決於儀器，也取決於控制點本身是否穩定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A network's accuracy depends not only on instruments but on whether the control points themselves are stable. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b097-v13-10","title":"控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性：定量估算","titleEn":"Monuments, pillars and point stability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「強制對心觀測墩」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Forced-centring pillars” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：對心誤差造成的角度誤差 ε = e/D。三腳架光學對心 e = 1 mm、後視距離 D = 50 m：ε = 0.001/50 = 20 µrad ≈ 4.1″；強制對心 e = 0.1 mm 時 ε ≈ 0.4″。以 4.1″ 的方向誤差放樣 200 m 外的點，橫向偏差 = 200×20×10⁻⁶ = 4.0 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Angular error from centring ε = e/D. Optical tripod centring with e = 1 mm and a 50 m backsight gives ε = 0.001/50 = 20 µrad ≈ 4.1″; forced centring with e = 0.1 mm gives ε ≈ 0.4″. Setting out a point 200 m away with a 4.1″ direction error displaces it laterally by 200×20×10⁻⁶ = 4.0 mm. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立控制點時拍照並記錄點之記（位置描述、埋設深度、周邊參考），開工前及每次重大開挖或降水前後重測控制點之間的距離與高差，與初始值比較；觀測墩可在不同時段重複量測，評估日照造成的微小移動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: When establishing control points photograph them and write point descriptions (location sketch, founding depth, nearby references); re-measure distances and height differences between control points before work starts and before and after major excavation or dewatering, comparing with initial values, and repeat pillar observations at different times of day to assess small solar movements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"對心誤差造成的角度誤差 ε = e/D。三腳架光學對心 e = 1 mm、後視距離 D = 50 m：ε = 0.001/50 = 20 µrad ≈ 4.1″；強制對心 e = 0.1 mm 時 ε ≈ 0.4″。以 4.1″ 的方向誤差放樣 200 m 外的點，橫向偏差 = 200×20×10⁻⁶ = 4.0 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Angular error from centring ε = e/D. Optical tripod centring with e = 1 mm and a 50 m backsight gives ε = 0.001/50 = 20 µrad ≈ 4.1″; forced centring with e = 0.1 mm gives ε ≈ 0.4″. Setting out a point 200 m away with a 4.1″ direction error displaces it laterally by 200×20×10⁻⁶ = 4.0 mm. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Monuments, pillars and point stability\", which statement holds?","options":["超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。","對心誤差造成的角度誤差 ε = e/D。","隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。"],"optionsEn":["A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment.","Angular error from centring ε = e/D.","If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對心誤差造成的角度誤差 ε = e/D。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Angular error from centring ε = e/D. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b097-v13-11","title":"控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Monuments, pillars and point stability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「強制對心觀測墩」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Forced-centring pillars” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立控制點時拍照並記錄點之記（位置描述、埋設深度、周邊參考），開工前及每次重大開挖或降水前後重測控制點之間的距離與高差，與初始值比較；觀測墩可在不同時段重複量測，評估日照造成的微小移動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"When establishing control points photograph them and write point descriptions (location sketch, founding depth, nearby references); re-measure distances and height differences between control points before work starts and before and after major excavation or dewatering, comparing with initial values, and repeat pillar observations at different times of day to assess small solar movements. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：控制點位置須由測量與大地工程人員共同選定，置於開挖影響範圍之外並加設保護；控制點遭碰撞或疑似移動時應立即停用並重新檢測，經測量主管確認後才能恢復使用。","observationEn":"Site practice: Control-point locations should be chosen jointly by survey and geotechnical staff, outside the zone of excavation influence and protected; any point that is struck or suspected of moving must be withdrawn immediately and re-checked, returning to use only after the survey lead confirms it.","failure":"注意干擾：主控制點設在基坑邊的臨時圍籬旁，隨著開挖與降水緩慢沉陷並向坑內位移，測量人員仍把它當成不動點，連續數月的放樣全部帶著同一系統偏差，直到與遠處參考點檢核才發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A primary point placed beside the temporary hoarding at the edge of an excavation slowly settles and moves toward the pit with digging and dewatering, while surveyors still treat it as fixed; months of set-out carry the same systematic error until a check against a distant reference point reveals it. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立控制點時拍照並記錄點之記（位置描述、埋設深度、周邊參考），開工前及每次重大開挖或降水前後重測控制點之間的距離與高差，與初始值比較；觀測墩可在不同時段重複量測，評估日照造成的微小移動。","textEn":"When establishing control points photograph them and write point descriptions (location sketch, founding depth, nearby references); re-measure distances and height differences between control points before work starts and before and after major excavation or dewatering, comparing with initial values, and repeat pillar observations at different times of day to assess small solar movements.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"控制點位置須由測量與大地工程人員共同選定，置於開挖影響範圍之外並加設保護；控制點遭碰撞或疑似移動時應立即停用並重新檢測，經測量主管確認後才能恢復使用。","textEn":"Control-point locations should be chosen jointly by survey and geotechnical staff, outside the zone of excavation influence and protected; any point that is struck or suspected of moving must be withdrawn immediately and re-checked, returning to use only after the survey lead confirms it.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Monuments, pillars and point stability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。","建立控制點時拍照並記錄點之記（位置描述、埋設深度、周邊參考），開工前及每次重大開挖或降水前後重測控制點之間的距離與高差，與初始值比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough.","When establishing control points photograph them and write point descriptions (location sketch, founding depth, nearby references)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立控制點時拍照並記錄點之記（位置描述、埋設深度、周邊參考），開工前及每次重大開挖或降水前後重測控制點之間的距離與高差，與初始值比較；觀測墩可在不同時段重複量測，評估日照造成的微小移動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"When establishing control points photograph them and write point descriptions (location sketch, founding depth, nearby references); re-measure distances and height differences between control points before work starts and before and after major excavation or dewatering, comparing with initial values, and repeat pillar observations at different times of day to assess small solar movements. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b097-v13-12","title":"控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Monuments, pillars and point stability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「強制對心觀測墩」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Forced-centring pillars” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"主控制點設在基坑邊的臨時圍籬旁，隨著開挖與降水緩慢沉陷並向坑內位移，測量人員仍把它當成不動點，連續數月的放樣全部帶著同一系統偏差，直到與遠處參考點檢核才發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A primary point placed beside the temporary hoarding at the edge of an excavation slowly settles and moves toward the pit with digging and dewatering, while surveyors still treat it as fixed; months of set-out carry the same systematic error until a check against a distant reference point reveals it. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：觀測墩本身也會受日照溫差與地下水變化而微小移動，所以重要工程會在影響範圍外另設參考點，用來判斷控制點是否移動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pillars also move slightly with solar heating and groundwater changes, so major works add reference points outside the zone of influence to judge whether control points have moved.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"主控制點設在基坑邊的臨時圍籬旁，隨著開挖與降水緩慢沉陷並向坑內位移，測量人員仍把它當成不動點，連續數月的放樣全部帶著同一系統偏差，直到與遠處參考點檢核才發現。","textEn":"A primary point placed beside the temporary hoarding at the edge of an excavation slowly settles and moves toward the pit with digging and dewatering, while surveyors still treat it as fixed; months of set-out carry the same systematic error until a check against a distant reference point reveals it.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制點標石、觀測墩與穩定性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Monuments, pillars and point stability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["主控制點設在基坑邊的臨時圍籬旁，隨著開挖與降水緩慢沉陷並向坑內位移，測量人員仍把它當成不動點，連續數月的放樣全部帶著同一系統偏差，直到與遠處參考點檢核才發現。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。"],"optionsEn":["A primary point placed beside the temporary hoarding at the edge of an excavation slowly settles and moves toward the pit with digging and dewatering, while surveyors still treat it as fixed.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主控制點設在基坑邊的臨時圍籬旁，隨著開挖與降水緩慢沉陷並向坑內位移，測量人員仍把它當成不動點，連續數月的放樣全部帶著同一系統偏差，直到與遠處參考點檢核才發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A primary point placed beside the temporary hoarding at the edge of an excavation slowly settles and moves toward the pit with digging and dewatering, while surveyors still treat it as fixed; months of set-out carry the same systematic error until a check against a distant reference point reveals it. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b097-v13-13","title":"儀器精度規格與現場檢定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Instrument specifications and field testing: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「全測站測距與大氣改正」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Total-station EDM and atmospheric correction” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"全測站以電子測距與角度編碼器量測，測距精度常寫成 a mm + b ppm：a 是與距離無關的固定誤差，b 是隨距離成比例的誤差。光波在空氣中的速度受溫度與氣壓影響，未做大氣改正時，溫度誤差約每 1°C 造成約 1 ppm 的距離誤差；稜鏡常數設錯則讓每個距離都帶固定偏差。ISO 17123 系列規定以簡易現場程序檢查全測站、水準儀與 GNSS 的實際重複精度，讓工地確認儀器在當天條件下仍適合任務。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「全測站測距與大氣改正」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A total station measures with electronic distance measurement and angle encoders, and distance accuracy is usually stated as a mm + b ppm: a is a fixed error independent of distance and b a proportional error. The speed of light in air depends on temperature and pressure, so without atmospheric correction a temperature error of about 1°C causes roughly 1 ppm of distance error, while a wrong prism constant puts a fixed offset on every distance. The ISO 17123 series sets simple field procedures to check the actual repeatability of total stations, levels and GNSS, so the site can confirm that an instrument still suits the task under the day's conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Total-station EDM and atmospheric correction” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：規格 ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) 在 400 m 時為 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) specification at 400 m gives 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「全測站測距與大氣改正」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Total-station EDM and atmospheric correction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-13-k1","title":"儀器精度規格與現場檢定","titleEn":"Instrument specifications and field testing","text":"全測站以電子測距與角度編碼器量測，測距精度常寫成 a mm + b ppm：a 是與距離無關的固定誤差，b 是隨距離成比例的誤差。光波在空氣中的速度受溫度與氣壓影響，未做大氣改正時，溫度誤差約每 1°C 造成約 1 ppm 的距離誤差；稜鏡常數設錯則讓每個距離都帶固定偏差。","textEn":"A total station measures with electronic distance measurement and angle encoders, and distance accuracy is usually stated as a mm + b ppm: a is a fixed error independent of distance and b a proportional error. The speed of light in air depends on temperature and pressure, so without atmospheric correction a temperature error of about 1°C causes roughly 1 ppm of distance error, while a wrong prism constant puts a fixed offset on every distance.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「儀器精度規格與現場檢定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Instrument specifications and field testing\" is correct?","options":["儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。","全測站以電子測距與角度編碼器量測，測距精度常寫成 a mm + b ppm：a 是與距離無關的固定誤差，b 是隨距離成比例的誤差。","閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。"],"optionsEn":["The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site.","A total station measures with electronic distance measurement and angle encoders, and distance accuracy is usually stated as a mm + b ppm: a is a fixed error independent of distance and b a proportional error.","A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"全測站以電子測距與角度編碼器量測，測距精度常寫成 a mm + b ppm：a 是與距離無關的固定誤差，b 是隨距離成比例的誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A total station measures with electronic distance measurement and angle encoders, and distance accuracy is usually stated as a mm + b ppm: a is a fixed error independent of distance and b a proportional error. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b097-v13-14","title":"儀器精度規格與現場檢定：定量估算","titleEn":"Instrument specifications and field testing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「全測站測距與大氣改正」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Total-station EDM and atmospheric correction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：規格 ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) 在 400 m 時為 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm。若輸入溫度比實際低 5°C 而未改正，約 5 ppm×400 m = 2.0 mm，大於儀器本身誤差；稜鏡常數錯 30 mm（例如 −30 與 0 混用）則每個距離都偏 30 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) specification at 400 m gives 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm. Entering a temperature 5°C too low without correction adds about 5 ppm×400 m = 2.0 mm, more than the instrument's own error, and a prism constant wrong by 30 mm (for example mixing −30 and 0) offsets every distance by 30 mm. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依 ISO 17123-5 在工地基線上以規定測回數量測，計算實驗標準差並與製造商規格比較；每天作業前檢查視準軸與指標差、稜鏡常數與大氣參數設定，儀器定期送校並保存校正證書。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Following ISO 17123-5, observe the prescribed number of sets on a site baseline, compute the experimental standard deviation and compare it with the manufacturer's specification; before each day's work check collimation and index errors, prism constant and atmospheric settings, and send instruments for periodic calibration with certificates kept on file.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"規格 ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) 在 400 m 時為 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm。若輸入溫度比實際低 5°C 而未改正，約 5 ppm×400 m = 2.0 mm，大於儀器本身誤差；稜鏡常數錯 30 mm（例如 −30 與 0 混用）則每個距離都偏 30 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) specification at 400 m gives 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm. Entering a temperature 5°C too low without correction adds about 5 ppm×400 m = 2.0 mm, more than the instrument's own error, and a prism constant wrong by 30 mm (for example mixing −30 and 0) offsets every distance by 30 mm. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「儀器精度規格與現場檢定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Instrument specifications and field testing\", which statement holds?","options":["GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。","監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。","規格 ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) 在 400 m 時為 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm。"],"optionsEn":["The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level.","Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points.","A ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) specification at 400 m gives 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"規格 ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) 在 400 m 時為 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A ±(1 mm + 1 ppm) specification at 400 m gives 1 + 400×10⁻⁶×1,000 = 1.4 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b097-v13-15","title":"儀器精度規格與現場檢定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Instrument specifications and field testing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「全測站測距與大氣改正」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Total-station EDM and atmospheric correction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依 ISO 17123-5 在工地基線上以規定測回數量測，計算實驗標準差並與製造商規格比較；每天作業前檢查視準軸與指標差、稜鏡常數與大氣參數設定，儀器定期送校並保存校正證書。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Following ISO 17123-5, observe the prescribed number of sets on a site baseline, compute the experimental standard deviation and compare it with the manufacturer's specification; before each day's work check collimation and index errors, prism constant and atmospheric settings, and send instruments for periodic calibration with certificates kept on file. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：測量作業程序應規定開工前的儀器現場檢定、每日檢查表、稜鏡與儀器配對清單及大氣量測方式；未通過檢定的儀器貼上停用標籤，經校正並由測量主管簽認後才能再用。","observationEn":"Site practice: The survey procedure should require field tests before work starts, a daily checklist, a register pairing prisms with instruments and the method of atmospheric measurement; an instrument that fails is tagged out of service and returns only after calibration and sign-off by the survey lead.","failure":"注意干擾：儀器從冷氣車廂直接拿到烈日下使用而未等待溫度平衡，大氣參數又沿用前一天的設定，整天的距離帶著數 ppm 的偏差；混用不同廠牌稜鏡卻未改常數，放樣點系統性偏移數公分。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An instrument taken straight from an air-conditioned vehicle into strong sun without time to equilibrate, with atmospheric settings carried over from the previous day, biases a whole day's distances by several ppm; mixing prism brands without changing the constant shifts set-out points systematically by centimetres. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依 ISO 17123-5 在工地基線上以規定測回數量測，計算實驗標準差並與製造商規格比較；每天作業前檢查視準軸與指標差、稜鏡常數與大氣參數設定，儀器定期送校並保存校正證書。","textEn":"Following ISO 17123-5, observe the prescribed number of sets on a site baseline, compute the experimental standard deviation and compare it with the manufacturer's specification; before each day's work check collimation and index errors, prism constant and atmospheric settings, and send instruments for periodic calibration with certificates kept on file.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"測量作業程序應規定開工前的儀器現場檢定、每日檢查表、稜鏡與儀器配對清單及大氣量測方式；未通過檢定的儀器貼上停用標籤，經校正並由測量主管簽認後才能再用。","textEn":"The survey procedure should require field tests before work starts, a daily checklist, a register pairing prisms with instruments and the method of atmospheric measurement; an instrument that fails is tagged out of service and returns only after calibration and sign-off by the survey lead.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「儀器精度規格與現場檢定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Instrument specifications and field testing\"?","options":["依 ISO 17123-5 在工地基線上以規定測回數量測，計算實驗標準差並與製造商規格比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。"],"optionsEn":["Following ISO 17123-5, observe the prescribed number of sets on a site baseline, compute the experimental standard deviation and compare it with the manufacturer's specification.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"依 ISO 17123-5 在工地基線上以規定測回數量測，計算實驗標準差並與製造商規格比較；每天作業前檢查視準軸與指標差、稜鏡常數與大氣參數設定，儀器定期送校並保存校正證書。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Following ISO 17123-5, observe the prescribed number of sets on a site baseline, compute the experimental standard deviation and compare it with the manufacturer's specification; before each day's work check collimation and index errors, prism constant and atmospheric settings, and send instruments for periodic calibration with certificates kept on file. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b097-v13-16","title":"儀器精度規格與現場檢定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Instrument specifications and field testing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「全測站測距與大氣改正」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Total-station EDM and atmospheric correction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"儀器從冷氣車廂直接拿到烈日下使用而未等待溫度平衡，大氣參數又沿用前一天的設定，整天的距離帶著數 ppm 的偏差；混用不同廠牌稜鏡卻未改常數，放樣點系統性偏移數公分。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An instrument taken straight from an air-conditioned vehicle into strong sun without time to equilibrate, with atmospheric settings carried over from the previous day, biases a whole day's distances by several ppm; mixing prism brands without changing the constant shifts set-out points systematically by centimetres. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：ISO 17123 系列規定以簡易現場程序檢查全測站、水準儀與 GNSS 的實際重複精度，讓工地確認儀器在當天條件下仍適合任務。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The ISO 17123 series sets simple field procedures to check the actual repeatability of total stations, levels and GNSS, so the site can confirm that an instrument still suits the task under the day's conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"儀器從冷氣車廂直接拿到烈日下使用而未等待溫度平衡，大氣參數又沿用前一天的設定，整天的距離帶著數 ppm 的偏差；混用不同廠牌稜鏡卻未改常數，放樣點系統性偏移數公分。","textEn":"An instrument taken straight from an air-conditioned vehicle into strong sun without time to equilibrate, with atmospheric settings carried over from the previous day, biases a whole day's distances by several ppm; mixing prism brands without changing the constant shifts set-out points systematically by centimetres.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「儀器精度規格與現場檢定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Instrument specifications and field testing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","儀器從冷氣車廂直接拿到烈日下使用而未等待溫度平衡，大氣參數又沿用前一天的設定，整天的距離帶著數 ppm 的偏差。","閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An instrument taken straight from an air-conditioned vehicle into strong sun without time to equilibrate, with atmospheric settings carried over from the previous day, biases a whole day's distances by several ppm.","A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"儀器從冷氣車廂直接拿到烈日下使用而未等待溫度平衡，大氣參數又沿用前一天的設定，整天的距離帶著數 ppm 的偏差；混用不同廠牌稜鏡卻未改常數，放樣點系統性偏移數公分。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An instrument taken straight from an air-conditioned vehicle into strong sun without time to equilibrate, with atmospheric settings carried over from the previous day, biases a whole day's distances by several ppm; mixing prism brands without changing the constant shifts set-out points systematically by centimetres. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b097-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「導線加密、網形平差與閉合差」與「高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure\" and \"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b097-v13-17","title":"導線加密、網形平差與閉合差：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「閉合導線與平差」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Closed traverse and adjustment” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主控制點之間距離較遠，施工需要的點要以導線或測站網加密：從已知點出發，逐站量測水平角與距離，最後閉合到另一已知點。閉合差反映整條導線的誤差累積並能顯示粗差；更嚴謹的做法是把所有觀測放入最小二乘網形平差，得到每個點的坐標、誤差橢圓與多餘觀測，並以統計檢定（例如資料探測）找出有問題的觀測。網形必須有足夠的多餘觀測，單一路徑的支導線無法檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「閉合導線與平差」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Primary points are far apart, so the points construction needs are densified by traverses or networks: starting from a known point, horizontal angles and distances are measured station by station, closing on another known point. The misclosure reflects the error accumulated along the traverse and reveals blunders; the more rigorous approach puts all observations into a least-squares network adjustment that gives coordinates, error ellipses and redundancy for every point, with statistical tests such as data snooping to find faulty observations. The network needs enough redundant observations, since a single open spur traverse cannot be checked. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Closed traverse and adjustment” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：閉合導線周長 1,200 m，坐標閉合差 ΔE = +0.012 m、ΔN = −0.009 m，線性閉合差 = √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m，相對精度 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A closed traverse 1,200 m long has coordinate misclosures ΔE = +0.012 m and ΔN = −0.009 m, so the linear misclosure is √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m and the relative precision is 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000.","failure":"常見誤解：「閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「閉合導線與平差」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Closed traverse and adjustment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-17-k1","title":"導線加密、網形平差與閉合差","titleEn":"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure","text":"主控制點之間距離較遠，施工需要的點要以導線或測站網加密：從已知點出發，逐站量測水平角與距離，最後閉合到另一已知點。閉合差反映整條導線的誤差累積並能顯示粗差；更嚴謹的做法是把所有觀測放入最小二乘網形平差，得到每個點的坐標、誤差橢圓與多餘觀測，並以統計檢定（例如資料探測）找出有問題的觀測。","textEn":"Primary points are far apart, so the points construction needs are densified by traverses or networks: starting from a known point, horizontal angles and distances are measured station by station, closing on another known point. The misclosure reflects the error accumulated along the traverse and reveals blunders; the more rigorous approach puts all observations into a least-squares network adjustment that gives coordinates, error ellipses and redundancy for every point, with statistical tests such as data snooping to find faulty observations.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導線加密、網形平差與閉合差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure\" is correct?","options":["閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。","超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。","主控制點之間距離較遠，施工需要的點要以導線或測站網加密：從已知點出發，逐站量測水平角與距離，最後閉合到另一已知點。"],"optionsEn":["A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors.","A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment.","Primary points are far apart, so the points construction needs are densified by traverses or networks: starting from a known point, horizontal angles and distances are measured station by station, closing on another known point."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主控制點之間距離較遠，施工需要的點要以導線或測站網加密：從已知點出發，逐站量測水平角與距離，最後閉合到另一已知點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Primary points are far apart, so the points construction needs are densified by traverses or networks: starting from a known point, horizontal angles and distances are measured station by station, closing on another known point. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b097-v13-18","title":"導線加密、網形平差與閉合差：定量估算","titleEn":"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「閉合導線與平差」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Closed traverse and adjustment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：閉合導線周長 1,200 m，坐標閉合差 ΔE = +0.012 m、ΔN = −0.009 m，線性閉合差 = √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m，相對精度 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000。8 個測站的角度閉合差容許值若取 5″√n = 5×√8 ≈ 14″，實測 9″ 即合格。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A closed traverse 1,200 m long has coordinate misclosures ΔE = +0.012 m and ΔN = −0.009 m, so the linear misclosure is √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m and the relative precision is 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000. If the angular tolerance for 8 stations is 5″√n = 5×√8 ≈ 14″, a measured 9″ passes. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：平差報告需列出每個觀測的殘差、標準化殘差與多餘觀測分量，標準化殘差超過約 3 的觀測要追查；成果點誤差橢圓的長半軸須小於精度目標，並由另一組人員以不同路徑檢測少數關鍵點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The adjustment report must list residuals, standardised residuals and redundancy numbers for every observation, and any standardised residual above about 3 is investigated; error-ellipse semi-major axes of the resulting points must be below the accuracy target, and a different crew re-checks a few key points by a different route.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"閉合導線周長 1,200 m，坐標閉合差 ΔE = +0.012 m、ΔN = −0.009 m，線性閉合差 = √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m，相對精度 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000。8 個測站的角度閉合差容許值若取 5″√n = 5×√8 ≈ 14″，實測 9″ 即合格。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A closed traverse 1,200 m long has coordinate misclosures ΔE = +0.012 m and ΔN = −0.009 m, so the linear misclosure is √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m and the relative precision is 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000. If the angular tolerance for 8 stations is 5″√n = 5×√8 ≈ 14″, a measured 9″ passes. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導線加密、網形平差與閉合差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure\", which statement holds?","options":["閉合導線周長 1,200 m，坐標閉合差 ΔE = +0.012 m、ΔN = −0.009 m，線性閉合差 = √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m，相對精度 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000。","隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。","坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["A closed traverse 1,200 m long has coordinate misclosures ΔE = +0.012 m and ΔN = −0.009 m, so the linear misclosure is √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m and the relative precision is 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000.","If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed.","Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"閉合導線周長 1,200 m，坐標閉合差 ΔE = +0.012 m、ΔN = −0.009 m，線性閉合差 = √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m，相對精度 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A closed traverse 1,200 m long has coordinate misclosures ΔE = +0.012 m and ΔN = −0.009 m, so the linear misclosure is √(0.012² + 0.009²) = 0.015 m and the relative precision is 0.015/1,200 = 1/80,000. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b097-v13-19","title":"導線加密、網形平差與閉合差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「閉合導線與平差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Closed traverse and adjustment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"平差報告需列出每個觀測的殘差、標準化殘差與多餘觀測分量，標準化殘差超過約 3 的觀測要追查；成果點誤差橢圓的長半軸須小於精度目標，並由另一組人員以不同路徑檢測少數關鍵點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The adjustment report must list residuals, standardised residuals and redundancy numbers for every observation, and any standardised residual above about 3 is investigated; error-ellipse semi-major axes of the resulting points must be below the accuracy target, and a different crew re-checks a few key points by a different route. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：控制加密一律採閉合導線或網形觀測，以最小二乘法平差並保存原始觀測檔；成果表需附平差報告並經測量主管簽核，未簽核的坐標不得用於放樣。","observationEn":"Site practice: Densify control only with closed traverses or network observations, adjust by least squares and keep the raw observation files; the coordinate list must come with the adjustment report signed by the survey lead, and unsigned coordinates may not be used for set-out.","failure":"注意干擾：為了趕工以多段支導線一路延伸到基地另一端，既無閉合也無檢核，某一站的後視點認錯導致後續所有點旋轉數十秒，偏差到最後一站已達數公分卻無人察覺。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rushing, a crew extends a chain of open spur traverses to the far end of the site with no closure or check; a wrong backsight at one station rotates every later point by tens of seconds, and the error reaches several centimetres at the last station without anyone noticing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"平差報告需列出每個觀測的殘差、標準化殘差與多餘觀測分量，標準化殘差超過約 3 的觀測要追查；成果點誤差橢圓的長半軸須小於精度目標，並由另一組人員以不同路徑檢測少數關鍵點。","textEn":"The adjustment report must list residuals, standardised residuals and redundancy numbers for every observation, and any standardised residual above about 3 is investigated; error-ellipse semi-major axes of the resulting points must be below the accuracy target, and a different crew re-checks a few key points by a different route.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"控制加密一律採閉合導線或網形觀測，以最小二乘法平差並保存原始觀測檔；成果表需附平差報告並經測量主管簽核，未簽核的坐標不得用於放樣。","textEn":"Densify control only with closed traverses or network observations, adjust by least squares and keep the raw observation files; the coordinate list must come with the adjustment report signed by the survey lead, and unsigned coordinates may not be used for set-out.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導線加密、網形平差與閉合差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","平差報告需列出每個觀測的殘差、標準化殘差與多餘觀測分量，標準化殘差超過約 3 的觀測要追查。","坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","The adjustment report must list residuals, standardised residuals and redundancy numbers for every observation, and any standardised residual above about 3 is investigated.","The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平差報告需列出每個觀測的殘差、標準化殘差與多餘觀測分量，標準化殘差超過約 3 的觀測要追查；成果點誤差橢圓的長半軸須小於精度目標，並由另一組人員以不同路徑檢測少數關鍵點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The adjustment report must list residuals, standardised residuals and redundancy numbers for every observation, and any standardised residual above about 3 is investigated; error-ellipse semi-major axes of the resulting points must be below the accuracy target, and a different crew re-checks a few key points by a different route. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b097-v13-20","title":"導線加密、網形平差與閉合差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「閉合導線與平差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Closed traverse and adjustment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為了趕工以多段支導線一路延伸到基地另一端，既無閉合也無檢核，某一站的後視點認錯導致後續所有點旋轉數十秒，偏差到最後一站已達數公分卻無人察覺。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rushing, a crew extends a chain of open spur traverses to the far end of the site with no closure or check; a wrong backsight at one station rotates every later point by tens of seconds, and the error reaches several centimetres at the last station without anyone noticing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：網形必須有足夠的多餘觀測，單一路徑的支導線無法檢查。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The network needs enough redundant observations, since a single open spur traverse cannot be checked.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為了趕工以多段支導線一路延伸到基地另一端，既無閉合也無檢核，某一站的後視點認錯導致後續所有點旋轉數十秒，偏差到最後一站已達數公分卻無人察覺。","textEn":"Rushing, a crew extends a chain of open spur traverses to the far end of the site with no closure or check; a wrong backsight at one station rotates every later point by tens of seconds, and the error reaches several centimetres at the last station without anyone noticing.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導線加密、網形平差與閉合差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Traverse densification, network adjustment and misclosure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。","為了趕工以多段支導線一路延伸到基地另一端，既無閉合也無檢核，某一站的後視點認錯導致後續所有點旋轉數十秒，偏差到最後一站已達數公分卻無人察覺。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment.","Rushing, a crew extends a chain of open spur traverses to the far end of the site with no closure or check."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為了趕工以多段支導線一路延伸到基地另一端，既無閉合也無檢核，某一站的後視點認錯導致後續所有點旋轉數十秒，偏差到最後一站已達數公分卻無人察覺。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rushing, a crew extends a chain of open spur traverses to the far end of the site with no closure or check; a wrong backsight at one station rotates every later point by tens of seconds, and the error reaches several centimetres at the last station without anyone noticing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b097-v13-21","title":"高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「樓板垂直傳遞孔」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Slab transfer openings” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"高層建築的軸線要從地面控制逐層往上傳：常用方式是在樓板預留垂直傳遞孔，以天頂垂準儀或雷射垂準儀把地面參考點投到上層，再在上層重建軸線。樓層越高，核心筒會因日照受熱不均而彎曲、因風擺動、因自重與潛變縮短，所以量測要選在清晨溫度均勻、風小的時段；超高層更在核心筒頂部以 GNSS 搭配傾斜儀修正瞬間擺動，並依設計提供的預調量施作，而不是追求當下的絕對垂直。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「樓板垂直傳遞孔」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Grid lines in a tall building are carried up floor by floor from ground control: transfer holes are left in the slabs and zenith or laser plummets project ground reference points to the upper floor, where the grid is re-established. The higher the building, the more the core bends from uneven solar heating, sways in wind and shortens under self-weight and creep, so observations are taken early in the morning when temperatures are even and wind is light; supertall towers also combine GNSS at the top of the core with inclinometers to correct instantaneous sway, and build to the pre-set offsets supplied by the designer rather than chasing momentary absolute verticality. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Slab transfer openings” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：核心筒兩側溫差造成的頂部側移 δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Top drift from a temperature difference across the core δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B).","failure":"常見誤解：「超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「樓板垂直傳遞孔」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Slab transfer openings”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-21-k1","title":"高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞","titleEn":"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings","text":"高層建築的軸線要從地面控制逐層往上傳：常用方式是在樓板預留垂直傳遞孔，以天頂垂準儀或雷射垂準儀把地面參考點投到上層，再在上層重建軸線。樓層越高，核心筒會因日照受熱不均而彎曲、因風擺動、因自重與潛變縮短，所以量測要選在清晨溫度均勻、風小的時段；超高層更在核心筒頂部以 GNSS 搭配傾斜儀修正瞬間擺動，並依設計提供的預調量施作，而不是追求當下的絕對垂直。","textEn":"Grid lines in a tall building are carried up floor by floor from ground control: transfer holes are left in the slabs and zenith or laser plummets project ground reference points to the upper floor, where the grid is re-established. The higher the building, the more the core bends from uneven solar heating, sways in wind and shortens under self-weight and creep, so observations are taken early in the morning when temperatures are even and wind is light; supertall towers also combine GNSS at the top of the core with inclinometers to correct instantaneous sway, and build to the pre-set offsets supplied by the designer rather than chasing momentary absolute verticality.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings\" is correct?","options":["高層建築的軸線要從地面控制逐層往上傳：常用方式是在樓板預留垂直傳遞孔，以天頂垂準儀或雷射垂準儀把地面參考點投到上層，再在上層重建軸線。","超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。","GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。"],"optionsEn":["Grid lines in a tall building are carried up floor by floor from ground control: transfer holes are left in the slabs and zenith or laser plummets project ground reference points to the upper floor, where the grid is re-established.","A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment.","The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高層建築的軸線要從地面控制逐層往上傳：常用方式是在樓板預留垂直傳遞孔，以天頂垂準儀或雷射垂準儀把地面參考點投到上層，再在上層重建軸線。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Grid lines in a tall building are carried up floor by floor from ground control: transfer holes are left in the slabs and zenith or laser plummets project ground reference points to the upper floor, where the grid is re-established. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b097-v13-22","title":"高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞：定量估算","titleEn":"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樓板垂直傳遞孔」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Slab transfer openings” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：核心筒兩側溫差造成的頂部側移 δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。取 α = 1.0×10⁻⁵/°C、ΔT = 5°C、高度 H = 300 m、寬度 B = 30 m：δ = 1.0×10⁻⁵×5×300²/(2×30) = 4.5/60 = 0.075 m = 75 mm。相較之下，每 30 m 接力一次、每次 ±1.5 mm 的垂準傳遞，10 次合成 √10×1.5 ≈ 4.7 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Top drift from a temperature difference across the core δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B). With α = 1.0×10⁻⁵/°C, ΔT = 5°C, height H = 300 m and width B = 30 m: δ = 1.0×10⁻⁵×5×300²/(2×30) = 4.5/60 = 0.075 m = 75 mm. By comparison, plumb transfers relayed every 30 m with ±1.5 mm each combine over 10 relays to √10×1.5 ≈ 4.7 mm. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每次傳遞後在上層以至少三個傳遞點檢查彼此的距離與角度，與地面值比較；高樓層同時以 GNSS 與傾斜儀記錄核心筒當時的偏移，換算回設計的理論位置，並定期由底層重新傳遞一次，避免接力誤差累積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each transfer, check distances and angles between at least three transferred points on the upper floor against their ground values; at high levels record the core's instantaneous offset with GNSS and inclinometers, convert back to the designer's theoretical position, and periodically re-transfer from the base to stop relay errors accumulating.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"核心筒兩側溫差造成的頂部側移 δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。取 α = 1.0×10⁻⁵/°C、ΔT = 5°C、高度 H = 300 m、寬度 B = 30 m：δ = 1.0×10⁻⁵×5×300²/(2×30) = 4.5/60 = 0.075 m = 75 mm。相較之下，每 30 m 接力一次、每次 ±1.5 mm 的垂準傳遞，10 次合成 √10×1.5 ≈ 4.7 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Top drift from a temperature difference across the core δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B). With α = 1.0×10⁻⁵/°C, ΔT = 5°C, height H = 300 m and width B = 30 m: δ = 1.0×10⁻⁵×5×300²/(2×30) = 4.5/60 = 0.075 m = 75 mm. By comparison, plumb transfers relayed every 30 m with ±1.5 mm each combine over 10 relays to √10×1.5 ≈ 4.7 mm. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings\", which statement holds?","options":["監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。","核心筒兩側溫差造成的頂部側移 δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。","只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。"],"optionsEn":["Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points.","Top drift from a temperature difference across the core δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B).","With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核心筒兩側溫差造成的頂部側移 δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Top drift from a temperature difference across the core δ ≈ α·ΔT·H²/(2B). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b097-v13-23","title":"高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樓板垂直傳遞孔」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Slab transfer openings” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每次傳遞後在上層以至少三個傳遞點檢查彼此的距離與角度，與地面值比較；高樓層同時以 GNSS 與傾斜儀記錄核心筒當時的偏移，換算回設計的理論位置，並定期由底層重新傳遞一次，避免接力誤差累積。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each transfer, check distances and angles between at least three transferred points on the upper floor against their ground values; at high levels record the core's instantaneous offset with GNSS and inclinometers, convert back to the designer's theoretical position, and periodically re-transfer from the base to stop relay errors accumulating. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：垂直傳遞作業程序要規定觀測時段、風速與溫差門檻、傳遞點數量與回到底層重新傳遞的間隔；預調量由結構設計者以書面提供，測量單位不得自行決定修正量。","observationEn":"Site practice: The vertical-transfer procedure should set observation windows, wind and temperature-difference limits, the number of transfer points and the interval for re-transferring from the base; pre-set offsets come in writing from the structural designer, and surveyors must not decide corrections on their own.","failure":"注意干擾：在午後日照強烈時做垂直傳遞，把核心筒暫時的熱彎曲當成施工偏差並在上層修正，第二天清晨結構回彎，軸線反而被修歪；長期只依賴下一層接力而不回到底層檢核，誤差逐層累積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A transfer made in strong afternoon sun treats temporary thermal bending of the core as construction error and corrects it on the upper floor; the next morning the structure straightens and the grid is now wrong. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每次傳遞後在上層以至少三個傳遞點檢查彼此的距離與角度，與地面值比較；高樓層同時以 GNSS 與傾斜儀記錄核心筒當時的偏移，換算回設計的理論位置，並定期由底層重新傳遞一次，避免接力誤差累積。","textEn":"After each transfer, check distances and angles between at least three transferred points on the upper floor against their ground values; at high levels record the core's instantaneous offset with GNSS and inclinometers, convert back to the designer's theoretical position, and periodically re-transfer from the base to stop relay errors accumulating.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"垂直傳遞作業程序要規定觀測時段、風速與溫差門檻、傳遞點數量與回到底層重新傳遞的間隔；預調量由結構設計者以書面提供，測量單位不得自行決定修正量。","textEn":"The vertical-transfer procedure should set observation windows, wind and temperature-difference limits, the number of transfer points and the interval for re-transferring from the base; pre-set offsets come in writing from the structural designer, and surveyors must not decide corrections on their own.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。","每次傳遞後在上層以至少三個傳遞點檢查彼此的距離與角度，與地面值比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change.","After each transfer, check distances and angles between at least three transferred points on the upper floor against their ground values."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每次傳遞後在上層以至少三個傳遞點檢查彼此的距離與角度，與地面值比較；高樓層同時以 GNSS 與傾斜儀記錄核心筒當時的偏移，換算回設計的理論位置，並定期由底層重新傳遞一次，避免接力誤差累積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each transfer, check distances and angles between at least three transferred points on the upper floor against their ground values; at high levels record the core's instantaneous offset with GNSS and inclinometers, convert back to the designer's theoretical position, and periodically re-transfer from the base to stop relay errors accumulating. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b097-v13-24","title":"高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樓板垂直傳遞孔」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Slab transfer openings” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在午後日照強烈時做垂直傳遞，把核心筒暫時的熱彎曲當成施工偏差並在上層修正，第二天清晨結構回彎，軸線反而被修歪；長期只依賴下一層接力而不回到底層檢核，誤差逐層累積。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A transfer made in strong afternoon sun treats temporary thermal bending of the core as construction error and corrects it on the upper floor; the next morning the structure straightens and the grid is now wrong. Relying for months on relays from the floor below without re-checking from the base lets errors accumulate floor by floor. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：樓層越高，核心筒會因日照受熱不均而彎曲、因風擺動、因自重與潛變縮短，所以量測要選在清晨溫度均勻、風小的時段；超高層更在核心筒頂部以 GNSS 搭配傾斜儀修正瞬間擺動，並依設計提供的預調量施作，而不是追求當下的絕對垂直。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The higher the building, the more the core bends from uneven solar heating, sways in wind and shortens under self-weight and creep, so observations are taken early in the morning when temperatures are even and wind is light; supertall towers also combine GNSS at the top of the core with inclinometers to correct instantaneous sway, and build to the pre-set offsets supplied by the designer rather than chasing momentary absolute verticality.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在午後日照強烈時做垂直傳遞，把核心筒暫時的熱彎曲當成施工偏差並在上層修正，第二天清晨結構回彎，軸線反而被修歪；長期只依賴下一層接力而不回到底層檢核，誤差逐層累積。","textEn":"A transfer made in strong afternoon sun treats temporary thermal bending of the core as construction error and corrects it on the upper floor; the next morning the structure straightens and the grid is now wrong. Relying for months on relays from the floor below without re-checking from the base lets errors accumulate floor by floor.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高層建築的軸線垂直傳遞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vertical transfer of grid lines in tall buildings\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["在午後日照強烈時做垂直傳遞，把核心筒暫時的熱彎曲當成施工偏差並在上層修正，第二天清晨結構回彎，軸線反而被修歪。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。"],"optionsEn":["A transfer made in strong afternoon sun treats temporary thermal bending of the core as construction error and corrects it on the upper floor.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在午後日照強烈時做垂直傳遞，把核心筒暫時的熱彎曲當成施工偏差並在上層修正，第二天清晨結構回彎，軸線反而被修歪；長期只依賴下一層接力而不回到底層檢核，誤差逐層累積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A transfer made in strong afternoon sun treats temporary thermal bending of the core as construction error and corrects it on the upper floor; the next morning the structure straightens and the grid is now wrong. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b097-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算」與「長隧道貫通與誤差傳播」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion\" and \"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b097-v13-25","title":"GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「GNSS 靜態基線」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “GNSS static baselines” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"GNSS 靜態測量在多個控制點同時長時間接收衛星訊號，以載波相位解算點與點之間的基線向量，精度可達公釐級，適合建立大範圍主控制網。為了避免同一組衛星幾何與大氣狀況造成的系統誤差，重要基線要在不同日期、不同時段重複觀測。GNSS 直接得到的是橢球高 h，工程需要的是以平均海水面為基準的正高 H，兩者相差大地起伏 N，必須以大地水準面模型換算，並以精密水準檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「GNSS 靜態基線」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A static GNSS survey records satellite signals at several control points simultaneously for long periods and solves baseline vectors between them from carrier phase, reaching millimetre-level precision suited to large primary networks. To avoid systematic errors from one satellite geometry and atmosphere, important baselines are re-observed on different days at different times. GNSS gives ellipsoidal height h directly, whereas works need orthometric height H referred to mean sea level; the two differ by the geoid undulation N, so a geoid model is used for conversion and precise levelling for checking. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “GNSS static baselines” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：H = h − N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: H = h − N.","failure":"常見誤解：「GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「GNSS 靜態基線」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “GNSS static baselines”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-25-k1","title":"GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算","titleEn":"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion","text":"GNSS 靜態測量在多個控制點同時長時間接收衛星訊號，以載波相位解算點與點之間的基線向量，精度可達公釐級，適合建立大範圍主控制網。為了避免同一組衛星幾何與大氣狀況造成的系統誤差，重要基線要在不同日期、不同時段重複觀測。","textEn":"A static GNSS survey records satellite signals at several control points simultaneously for long periods and solves baseline vectors between them from carrier phase, reaching millimetre-level precision suited to large primary networks. To avoid systematic errors from one satellite geometry and atmosphere, important baselines are re-observed on different days at different times.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion\" is correct?","options":["GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。","GNSS 靜態測量在多個控制點同時長時間接收衛星訊號，以載波相位解算點與點之間的基線向量，精度可達公釐級，適合建立大範圍主控制網。","隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。"],"optionsEn":["The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level.","A static GNSS survey records satellite signals at several control points simultaneously for long periods and solves baseline vectors between them from carrier phase, reaching millimetre-level precision suited to large primary networks.","If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"GNSS 靜態測量在多個控制點同時長時間接收衛星訊號，以載波相位解算點與點之間的基線向量，精度可達公釐級，適合建立大範圍主控制網。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A static GNSS survey records satellite signals at several control points simultaneously for long periods and solves baseline vectors between them from carrier phase, reaching millimetre-level precision suited to large primary networks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b097-v13-26","title":"GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「GNSS 靜態基線」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “GNSS static baselines” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：H = h − N。某點 GNSS 橢球高 h = 52.318 m、模型大地起伏 N = 21.740 m，H = 52.318 − 21.740 = 30.578 m。精密水準 2 km 閉合路線若容許 3 mm√K = 3×√2 ≈ 4.2 mm，而 GNSS 推得高程與水準相差 18 mm：雖在約 2 cm 的大地水準面模型不確定度內，仍超出水準容許值，施工高程應以水準為準。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: H = h − N. With GNSS ellipsoidal height h = 52.318 m and model undulation N = 21.740 m, H = 52.318 − 21.740 = 30.578 m. If a 2 km precise-levelling loop allows 3 mm√K = 3×√2 ≈ 4.2 mm and the GNSS-derived height differs from levelling by 18 mm, it lies within a geoid-model uncertainty of about 2 cm yet beyond the levelling tolerance, so construction heights should follow levelling. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：參考 NOAA NGS-58 一類指引：每條相鄰基線至少在兩個不同日期、不同時段觀測，重複高差超過門檻就重測；網形平差時檢查基線閉合環，最後以精密水準聯測數個 GNSS 點，比較換算正高與水準高程，確認大地水準面模型在本地適用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Following guidance such as NOAA NGS-58, observe every adjacent baseline on at least two different days at different times and re-observe when repeat height differences exceed the threshold; check baseline loop closures in the network adjustment, and finally tie several GNSS points by precise levelling to compare converted orthometric heights with levelled heights, confirming that the geoid model fits locally.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"H = h − N。某點 GNSS 橢球高 h = 52.318 m、模型大地起伏 N = 21.740 m，H = 52.318 − 21.740 = 30.578 m。精密水準 2 km 閉合路線若容許 3 mm√K = 3×√2 ≈ 4.2 mm，而 GNSS 推得高程與水準相差 18 mm：雖在約 2 cm 的大地水準面模型不確定度內，仍超出水準容許值，施工高程應以水準為準。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"H = h − N. With GNSS ellipsoidal height h = 52.318 m and model undulation N = 21.740 m, H = 52.318 − 21.740 = 30.578 m. If a 2 km precise-levelling loop allows 3 mm√K = 3×√2 ≈ 4.2 mm and the GNSS-derived height differs from levelling by 18 mm, it lies within a geoid-model uncertainty of about 2 cm yet beyond the levelling tolerance, so construction heights should follow levelling. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。","坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。","H = h − N。"],"optionsEn":["Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough.","The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground.","H = h − N."],"answer":2,"explanation":"H = h − N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"H = h − N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b097-v13-27","title":"GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「GNSS 靜態基線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “GNSS static baselines” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"參考 NOAA NGS-58 一類指引：每條相鄰基線至少在兩個不同日期、不同時段觀測，重複高差超過門檻就重測；網形平差時檢查基線閉合環，最後以精密水準聯測數個 GNSS 點，比較換算正高與水準高程，確認大地水準面模型在本地適用。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Following guidance such as NOAA NGS-58, observe every adjacent baseline on at least two different days at different times and re-observe when repeat height differences exceed the threshold; check baseline loop closures in the network adjustment, and finally tie several GNSS points by precise levelling to compare converted orthometric heights with levelled heights, confirming that the geoid model fits locally. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：主控制網一律採靜態 GNSS 加重複觀測並與國家控制點聯測，高程以精密水準傳遞；RTK 只用於次級控制與碎部，且每天開工前先在已知點上檢核。","observationEn":"Site practice: Establish primary control only by static GNSS with repeat sessions tied to national control points, carry heights by precise levelling, and use RTK only for secondary control and detail, checking it on a known point before each day's work.","failure":"注意干擾：以單次短時間 RTK 量測建立主控制，未做重複觀測，又把橢球高直接當作正高使用，結果基地兩端的高程基準相差數十公分，排水坡度與結構標高全部出錯。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Establishing primary control from single short RTK occupations without repeats, and using ellipsoidal height directly as orthometric height, leaves the height datum at the two ends of the site tens of centimetres apart, so drainage falls and structural levels are all wrong. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"參考 NOAA NGS-58 一類指引：每條相鄰基線至少在兩個不同日期、不同時段觀測，重複高差超過門檻就重測；網形平差時檢查基線閉合環，最後以精密水準聯測數個 GNSS 點，比較換算正高與水準高程，確認大地水準面模型在本地適用。","textEn":"Following guidance such as NOAA NGS-58, observe every adjacent baseline on at least two different days at different times and re-observe when repeat height differences exceed the threshold; check baseline loop closures in the network adjustment, and finally tie several GNSS points by precise levelling to compare converted orthometric heights with levelled heights, confirming that the geoid model fits locally.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"主控制網一律採靜態 GNSS 加重複觀測並與國家控制點聯測，高程以精密水準傳遞；RTK 只用於次級控制與碎部，且每天開工前先在已知點上檢核。","textEn":"Establish primary control only by static GNSS with repeat sessions tied to national control points, carry heights by precise levelling, and use RTK only for secondary control and detail, checking it on a known point before each day's work.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion\"?","options":["參考 NOAA NGS-58 一類指引：每條相鄰基線至少在兩個不同日期、不同時段觀測，重複高差超過門檻就重測。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。"],"optionsEn":["Following guidance such as NOAA NGS-58, observe every adjacent baseline on at least two different days at different times and re-observe when repeat height differences exceed the threshold.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site."],"answer":0,"explanation":"參考 NOAA NGS-58 一類指引：每條相鄰基線至少在兩個不同日期、不同時段觀測，重複高差超過門檻就重測；網形平差時檢查基線閉合環，最後以精密水準聯測數個 GNSS 點，比較換算正高與水準高程，確認大地水準面模型在本地適用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Following guidance such as NOAA NGS-58, observe every adjacent baseline on at least two different days at different times and re-observe when repeat height differences exceed the threshold; check baseline loop closures in the network adjustment, and finally tie several GNSS points by precise levelling to compare converted orthometric heights with levelled heights, confirming that the geoid model fits locally. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b097-v13-28","title":"GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「GNSS 靜態基線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “GNSS static baselines” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以單次短時間 RTK 量測建立主控制，未做重複觀測，又把橢球高直接當作正高使用，結果基地兩端的高程基準相差數十公分，排水坡度與結構標高全部出錯。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Establishing primary control from single short RTK occupations without repeats, and using ellipsoidal height directly as orthometric height, leaves the height datum at the two ends of the site tens of centimetres apart, so drainage falls and structural levels are all wrong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：GNSS 直接得到的是橢球高 h，工程需要的是以平均海水面為基準的正高 H，兩者相差大地起伏 N，必須以大地水準面模型換算，並以精密水準檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: GNSS gives ellipsoidal height h directly, whereas works need orthometric height H referred to mean sea level; the two differ by the geoid undulation N, so a geoid model is used for conversion and precise levelling for checking.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以單次短時間 RTK 量測建立主控制，未做重複觀測，又把橢球高直接當作正高使用，結果基地兩端的高程基準相差數十公分，排水坡度與結構標高全部出錯。","textEn":"Establishing primary control from single short RTK occupations without repeats, and using ellipsoidal height directly as orthometric height, leaves the height datum at the two ends of the site tens of centimetres apart, so drainage falls and structural levels are all wrong.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「GNSS 靜態測量與高程換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Static GNSS surveys and height conversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以單次短時間 RTK 量測建立主控制，未做重複觀測，又把橢球高直接當作正高使用，結果基地兩端的高程基準相差數十公分，排水坡度與結構標高全部出錯。","隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Establishing primary control from single short RTK occupations without repeats, and using ellipsoidal height directly as orthometric height, leaves the height datum at the two ends of the site tens of centimetres apart, so drainage falls and structural levels are all wrong.","If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以單次短時間 RTK 量測建立主控制，未做重複觀測，又把橢球高直接當作正高使用，結果基地兩端的高程基準相差數十公分，排水坡度與結構標高全部出錯。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Establishing primary control from single short RTK occupations without repeats, and using ellipsoidal height directly as orthometric height, leaves the height datum at the two ends of the site tens of centimetres apart, so drainage falls and structural levels are all wrong. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b097-v13-29","title":"長隧道貫通與誤差傳播：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「隧道貫通誤差」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tunnel breakthrough error” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"長隧道從兩端或多個工作面對向開挖，洞內只能以導線向前延伸，沒有外部檢核，誤差隨長度累積，其中方位角誤差造成的橫向偏差隨距離線性放大。因此隧道測量要先在洞口建立高精度地面網，洞內採雙重導線、以陀螺經緯儀獨立定向並定期回測，才能把貫通偏差控制在公分級。戈達基線隧道東管 2010 年貫通時橫向偏差約 8 cm、垂直約 1 cm；1990 年英法海底隧道服務隧道貫通時約偏 30 cm 與 8 cm。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隧道貫通誤差」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A long tunnel is driven from both ends or several faces toward each other, and underground the control can only be extended by traverse with no outside check, so errors accumulate with length; lateral deviation from azimuth error grows linearly with distance. Tunnel surveys therefore begin with a high-accuracy surface network at the portals, then use double traverses underground, independent orientation by gyro-theodolite and regular re-measurement to hold the breakthrough deviation to centimetres. The east tube of the Gotthard Base Tunnel broke through in 2010 with about 8 cm lateral and 1 cm vertical deviation; the Channel Tunnel service tunnel met in 1990 about 30 cm and 8 cm apart. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Tunnel breakthrough error” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：方位角誤差 σ_α 造成的橫向偏差 e = L·σ_α。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Lateral deviation from azimuth error σ_α is e = L·σ_α.","failure":"常見誤解：「隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隧道貫通誤差」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Tunnel breakthrough error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-29-k1","title":"長隧道貫通與誤差傳播","titleEn":"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation","text":"長隧道從兩端或多個工作面對向開挖，洞內只能以導線向前延伸，沒有外部檢核，誤差隨長度累積，其中方位角誤差造成的橫向偏差隨距離線性放大。因此隧道測量要先在洞口建立高精度地面網，洞內採雙重導線、以陀螺經緯儀獨立定向並定期回測，才能把貫通偏差控制在公分級。","textEn":"A long tunnel is driven from both ends or several faces toward each other, and underground the control can only be extended by traverse with no outside check, so errors accumulate with length; lateral deviation from azimuth error grows linearly with distance. Tunnel surveys therefore begin with a high-accuracy surface network at the portals, then use double traverses underground, independent orientation by gyro-theodolite and regular re-measurement to hold the breakthrough deviation to centimetres.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長隧道貫通與誤差傳播」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation\" is correct?","options":["隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。","監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。","長隧道從兩端或多個工作面對向開挖，洞內只能以導線向前延伸，沒有外部檢核，誤差隨長度累積，其中方位角誤差造成的橫向偏差隨距離線性放大。"],"optionsEn":["If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed.","Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points.","A long tunnel is driven from both ends or several faces toward each other, and underground the control can only be extended by traverse with no outside check, so errors accumulate with length."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長隧道從兩端或多個工作面對向開挖，洞內只能以導線向前延伸，沒有外部檢核，誤差隨長度累積，其中方位角誤差造成的橫向偏差隨距離線性放大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A long tunnel is driven from both ends or several faces toward each other, and underground the control can only be extended by traverse with no outside check, so errors accumulate with length; lateral deviation from azimuth error grows linearly with distance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b097-v13-30","title":"長隧道貫通與誤差傳播：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隧道貫通誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tunnel breakthrough error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：方位角誤差 σ_α 造成的橫向偏差 e = L·σ_α。開挖 10 km、σ_α = 1″ = 4.85×10⁻⁶ rad：e = 10,000×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.049 m；σ_α = 2″ 時約 0.097 m。若每 2 km 以陀螺經緯儀獨立定向，且定向本身誤差可忽略，有效累積長度減為 2 km，1″ 對應的偏差僅約 2,000×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.010 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Lateral deviation from azimuth error σ_α is e = L·σ_α. Over a 10 km drive with σ_α = 1″ = 4.85×10⁻⁶ rad, e = 10,000×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.049 m; with σ_α = 2″ it is about 0.097 m. If a gyro-theodolite orientation every 2 km, itself of negligible error, cuts the effective accumulation length to 2 km, 1″ gives only about 2,000×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.010 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：貫通前由獨立團隊沿獨立路線重測洞內控制並與施工測量比較；貫通後量測兩端導線在貫通點的坐標差與高差，與預估的貫通誤差（例如 95% 信賴的誤差橢圓）比較，並據以調整最後一段的線形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before breakthrough, re-survey the underground control along an independent route by an independent team and compare it with the construction survey; after breakthrough, measure the coordinate and height differences between the two traverses at the meeting point, compare them with the predicted breakthrough error (for example the 95% error ellipse), and adjust the alignment of the final section accordingly.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"方位角誤差 σ_α 造成的橫向偏差 e = L·σ_α。開挖 10 km、σ_α = 1″ = 4.85×10⁻⁶ rad：e = 10,000×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.049 m；σ_α = 2″ 時約 0.097 m。若每 2 km 以陀螺經緯儀獨立定向，且定向本身誤差可忽略，有效累積長度減為 2 km，1″ 對應的偏差僅約 2,000×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.010 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Lateral deviation from azimuth error σ_α is e = L·σ_α. Over a 10 km drive with σ_α = 1″ = 4.85×10⁻⁶ rad, e = 10,000×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.049 m; with σ_α = 2″ it is about 0.097 m. If a gyro-theodolite orientation every 2 km, itself of negligible error, cuts the effective accumulation length to 2 km, 1″ gives only about 2,000×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 0.010 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長隧道貫通與誤差傳播」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation\", which statement holds?","options":["方位角誤差 σ_α 造成的橫向偏差 e = L·σ_α。","只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。","控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。"],"optionsEn":["Lateral deviation from azimuth error σ_α is e = L·σ_α.","With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation.","Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"方位角誤差 σ_α 造成的橫向偏差 e = L·σ_α。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Lateral deviation from azimuth error σ_α is e = L·σ_α. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b097-v13-31","title":"長隧道貫通與誤差傳播：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隧道貫通誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tunnel breakthrough error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"貫通前由獨立團隊沿獨立路線重測洞內控制並與施工測量比較；貫通後量測兩端導線在貫通點的坐標差與高差，與預估的貫通誤差（例如 95% 信賴的誤差橢圓）比較，並據以調整最後一段的線形。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before breakthrough, re-survey the underground control along an independent route by an independent team and compare it with the construction survey; after breakthrough, measure the coordinate and height differences between the two traverses at the meeting point, compare them with the predicted breakthrough error (for example the 95% error ellipse), and adjust the alignment of the final section accordingly. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：長隧道的測量設計要事先計算貫通誤差預算，規定陀螺定向間隔與獨立檢測時點；貫通前的最後檢測是保留點，須經業主的測量顧問確認後才能推進最後一段。","observationEn":"Site practice: The survey design for a long tunnel must compute a breakthrough error budget in advance and set gyro-orientation intervals and independent check stages; the final pre-breakthrough check is a hold point that the owner's survey consultant must accept before the last section is driven.","failure":"注意干擾：洞內導線貼近隧道壁布設，視線掠過壁面產生側向折射，誤差在每一站朝同一方向累積；沒有陀螺定向檢核時，貫通偏差可能遠大於預估，需以額外開挖或修改襯砌補救。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An underground traverse run close to the tunnel wall suffers lateral refraction as sight lines graze the wall, so errors accumulate in one direction at every station; without gyro checks the breakthrough deviation can far exceed the prediction and must be corrected by extra excavation or lining changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"貫通前由獨立團隊沿獨立路線重測洞內控制並與施工測量比較；貫通後量測兩端導線在貫通點的坐標差與高差，與預估的貫通誤差（例如 95% 信賴的誤差橢圓）比較，並據以調整最後一段的線形。","textEn":"Before breakthrough, re-survey the underground control along an independent route by an independent team and compare it with the construction survey; after breakthrough, measure the coordinate and height differences between the two traverses at the meeting point, compare them with the predicted breakthrough error (for example the 95% error ellipse), and adjust the alignment of the final section accordingly.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"長隧道的測量設計要事先計算貫通誤差預算，規定陀螺定向間隔與獨立檢測時點；貫通前的最後檢測是保留點，須經業主的測量顧問確認後才能推進最後一段。","textEn":"The survey design for a long tunnel must compute a breakthrough error budget in advance and set gyro-orientation intervals and independent check stages; the final pre-breakthrough check is a hold point that the owner's survey consultant must accept before the last section is driven.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長隧道貫通與誤差傳播」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","貫通前由獨立團隊沿獨立路線重測洞內控制並與施工測量比較。","閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Before breakthrough, re-survey the underground control along an independent route by an independent team and compare it with the construction survey.","A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"貫通前由獨立團隊沿獨立路線重測洞內控制並與施工測量比較；貫通後量測兩端導線在貫通點的坐標差與高差，與預估的貫通誤差（例如 95% 信賴的誤差橢圓）比較，並據以調整最後一段的線形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before breakthrough, re-survey the underground control along an independent route by an independent team and compare it with the construction survey; after breakthrough, measure the coordinate and height differences between the two traverses at the meeting point, compare them with the predicted breakthrough error (for example the 95% error ellipse), and adjust the alignment of the final section accordingly. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b097-v13-32","title":"長隧道貫通與誤差傳播：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隧道貫通誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tunnel breakthrough error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"洞內導線貼近隧道壁布設，視線掠過壁面產生側向折射，誤差在每一站朝同一方向累積；沒有陀螺定向檢核時，貫通偏差可能遠大於預估，需以額外開挖或修改襯砌補救。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An underground traverse run close to the tunnel wall suffers lateral refraction as sight lines graze the wall, so errors accumulate in one direction at every station; without gyro checks the breakthrough deviation can far exceed the prediction and must be corrected by extra excavation or lining changes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：戈達基線隧道東管 2010 年貫通時橫向偏差約 8 cm、垂直約 1 cm；1990 年英法海底隧道服務隧道貫通時約偏 30 cm 與 8 cm。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The east tube of the Gotthard Base Tunnel broke through in 2010 with about 8 cm lateral and 1 cm vertical deviation; the Channel Tunnel service tunnel met in 1990 about 30 cm and 8 cm apart.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隧道內導線只要每站量得夠準，就不需要獨立定向檢核。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If each underground traverse station is measured precisely enough, no independent orientation check is needed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"洞內導線貼近隧道壁布設，視線掠過壁面產生側向折射，誤差在每一站朝同一方向累積；沒有陀螺定向檢核時，貫通偏差可能遠大於預估，需以額外開挖或修改襯砌補救。","textEn":"An underground traverse run close to the tunnel wall suffers lateral refraction as sight lines graze the wall, so errors accumulate in one direction at every station; without gyro checks the breakthrough deviation can far exceed the prediction and must be corrected by extra excavation or lining changes.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長隧道貫通與誤差傳播」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-tunnel breakthrough and error propagation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。","洞內導線貼近隧道壁布設，視線掠過壁面產生側向折射，誤差在每一站朝同一方向累積；沒有陀螺定向檢核時，貫通偏差可能遠大於預估，需以額外開挖或修改襯砌補救。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points.","An underground traverse run close to the tunnel wall suffers lateral refraction as sight lines graze the wall, so errors accumulate in one direction at every station."],"answer":2,"explanation":"洞內導線貼近隧道壁布設，視線掠過壁面產生側向折射，誤差在每一站朝同一方向累積；沒有陀螺定向檢核時，貫通偏差可能遠大於預估，需以額外開挖或修改襯砌補救。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An underground traverse run close to the tunnel wall suffers lateral refraction as sight lines graze the wall, so errors accumulate in one direction at every station; without gyro checks the breakthrough deviation can far exceed the prediction and must be corrected by extra excavation or lining changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b097-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網複測與移動判定」與「控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Network re-survey and movement testing\" and \"Control records, reference frames and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b097-v13-33","title":"控制網複測與移動判定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Network re-survey and movement testing: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「參考點穩定性檢定」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reference-point stability test” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"施工期間控制網本身也會變形：開挖、降水、重車與鄰近結構沉陷都可能讓控制點移動，若繼續以舊坐標放樣或監測，就會把控制點的移動誤認為結構的移動。因此控制網要定期複測，並以統計檢定區分真正的移動與量測雜訊。Crossrail 的自動化監測經驗也指出，參考稜鏡應設在影響範圍外並分散於各方向，平差不應過度修改原始觀測，以免掩蓋網形衰退。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「參考點穩定性檢定」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The control network itself deforms during construction: excavation, dewatering, heavy traffic and settling neighbours can all move control points, and if set-out or monitoring continues on old coordinates, control movement is mistaken for structural movement. The network must therefore be re-surveyed periodically, with statistical tests that separate real movement from measurement noise. Crossrail's automated monitoring experience likewise found that reference prisms should sit outside the zone of influence and be spread in many directions, and that adjustments should change raw observations as little as possible so that network decay is not hidden. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Reference-point stability test” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：兩期坐標差 d = 4.0 mm，每期每一坐標分量標準差 σ = 1.2 mm，差值標準差 σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm，檢定量 d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 > 1.96，在 95% 信賴水準下判定為顯著移動；若 d = 2.0 mm，2.0/1.7 ≈ 1.18，不顯著。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Between two epochs a point differs by d = 4.0 mm with σ = 1.2 mm per coordinate component in each epoch, so σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm and the test statistic d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 exceeds 1.96, a significant movement at 95% confidence; with d = 2.0 mm, 2.0/1.7 ≈ 1.18 is not significant.","failure":"常見誤解：「監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「參考點穩定性檢定」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Reference-point stability test”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-33-k1","title":"控制網複測與移動判定","titleEn":"Network re-survey and movement testing","text":"施工期間控制網本身也會變形：開挖、降水、重車與鄰近結構沉陷都可能讓控制點移動，若繼續以舊坐標放樣或監測，就會把控制點的移動誤認為結構的移動。因此控制網要定期複測，並以統計檢定區分真正的移動與量測雜訊。","textEn":"The control network itself deforms during construction: excavation, dewatering, heavy traffic and settling neighbours can all move control points, and if set-out or monitoring continues on old coordinates, control movement is mistaken for structural movement. The network must therefore be re-surveyed periodically, with statistical tests that separate real movement from measurement noise.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網複測與移動判定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Network re-survey and movement testing\" is correct?","options":["施工期間控制網本身也會變形：開挖、降水、重車與鄰近結構沉陷都可能讓控制點移動，若繼續以舊坐標放樣或監測，就會把控制點的移動誤認為結構的移動。","監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。","坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["The control network itself deforms during construction: excavation, dewatering, heavy traffic and settling neighbours can all move control points, and if set-out or monitoring continues on old coordinates, control movement is mistaken for structural movement.","Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points.","Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工期間控制網本身也會變形：開挖、降水、重車與鄰近結構沉陷都可能讓控制點移動，若繼續以舊坐標放樣或監測，就會把控制點的移動誤認為結構的移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The control network itself deforms during construction: excavation, dewatering, heavy traffic and settling neighbours can all move control points, and if set-out or monitoring continues on old coordinates, control movement is mistaken for structural movement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b097-v13-34","title":"控制網複測與移動判定：定量估算","titleEn":"Network re-survey and movement testing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「參考點穩定性檢定」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reference-point stability test” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：兩期坐標差 d = 4.0 mm，每期每一坐標分量標準差 σ = 1.2 mm，差值標準差 σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm，檢定量 d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 > 1.96，在 95% 信賴水準下判定為顯著移動；若 d = 2.0 mm，2.0/1.7 ≈ 1.18，不顯著。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Between two epochs a point differs by d = 4.0 mm with σ = 1.2 mm per coordinate component in each epoch, so σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm and the test statistic d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 exceeds 1.96, a significant movement at 95% confidence; with d = 2.0 mm, 2.0/1.7 ≈ 1.18 is not significant. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依施工進度訂定複測頻率（例如每月一次，重大開挖前後加測），以相同儀器與網形重測，做自由網或以已證實穩定的點平差，逐點做顯著性檢定；判定移動的點要更新坐標並通知所有使用者，同時作廢舊坐標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Set re-survey frequency by construction progress (for example monthly, with extra surveys before and after major excavation), re-observe with the same instruments and geometry, adjust as a free network or on proven-stable points, and test every point for significance; points found to have moved get new coordinates that are issued to every user, with the old values withdrawn.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"兩期坐標差 d = 4.0 mm，每期每一坐標分量標準差 σ = 1.2 mm，差值標準差 σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm，檢定量 d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 > 1.96，在 95% 信賴水準下判定為顯著移動；若 d = 2.0 mm，2.0/1.7 ≈ 1.18，不顯著。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Between two epochs a point differs by d = 4.0 mm with σ = 1.2 mm per coordinate component in each epoch, so σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm and the test statistic d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 exceeds 1.96, a significant movement at 95% confidence; with d = 2.0 mm, 2.0/1.7 ≈ 1.18 is not significant. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網複測與移動判定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Network re-survey and movement testing\", which statement holds?","options":["坐標反算的距離就是現場量到的實際距離。","兩期坐標差 d = 4.0 mm，每期每一坐標分量標準差 σ = 1.2 mm，差值標準差 σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm，檢定量 d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 > 1.96，在 95% 信賴水準下判定為顯著移動。","儀器規格表上的精度，就是現場實際能達到的精度。"],"optionsEn":["The distance computed from coordinates equals the actual distance measured on the ground.","Between two epochs a point differs by d = 4.0 mm with σ = 1.2 mm per coordinate component in each epoch, so σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm and the test statistic d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 exceeds 1.96, a significant movement at 95% confidence.","The accuracy on the instrument data sheet is what will be achieved on site."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩期坐標差 d = 4.0 mm，每期每一坐標分量標準差 σ = 1.2 mm，差值標準差 σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm，檢定量 d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 > 1.96，在 95% 信賴水準下判定為顯著移動；若 d = 2.0 mm，2.0/1.7 ≈ 1.18，不顯著。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Between two epochs a point differs by d = 4.0 mm with σ = 1.2 mm per coordinate component in each epoch, so σ_d = √2×1.2 ≈ 1.7 mm and the test statistic d/σ_d = 4.0/1.7 ≈ 2.35 exceeds 1.96, a significant movement at 95% confidence; with d = 2.0 mm, 2.0/1.7 ≈ 1.18 is not significant. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b097-v13-35","title":"控制網複測與移動判定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Network re-survey and movement testing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「參考點穩定性檢定」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reference-point stability test” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依施工進度訂定複測頻率（例如每月一次，重大開挖前後加測），以相同儀器與網形重測，做自由網或以已證實穩定的點平差，逐點做顯著性檢定；判定移動的點要更新坐標並通知所有使用者，同時作廢舊坐標。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Set re-survey frequency by construction progress (for example monthly, with extra surveys before and after major excavation), re-observe with the same instruments and geometry, adjust as a free network or on proven-stable points, and test every point for significance; points found to have moved get new coordinates that are issued to every user, with the old values withdrawn. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：控制網複測成果要以版本編號發布並記錄生效日期，所有放樣與監測系統須在同一天切換到新版坐標；參考點的選定與更換須經監測工程師與大地工程師共同核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: Issue re-surveyed control coordinates under a version number with an effective date, and switch every set-out and monitoring system to the new version on the same day; selection and replacement of reference points need joint approval of the monitoring engineer and the geotechnical engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：監測站的參考稜鏡裝在會隨施工下沉的鄰近建物上，平差把參考點的沉陷平均分配到監測點，報表顯示軌道變位很小，實際沉陷卻被低估，警戒值觸發延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reference prisms for a monitoring station are fixed to neighbouring buildings that settle with the works; the adjustment spreads the reference settlement over the monitored points, reports show small track movements, real settlement is underestimated and alarm triggers come late. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依施工進度訂定複測頻率（例如每月一次，重大開挖前後加測），以相同儀器與網形重測，做自由網或以已證實穩定的點平差，逐點做顯著性檢定；判定移動的點要更新坐標並通知所有使用者，同時作廢舊坐標。","textEn":"Set re-survey frequency by construction progress (for example monthly, with extra surveys before and after major excavation), re-observe with the same instruments and geometry, adjust as a free network or on proven-stable points, and test every point for significance; points found to have moved get new coordinates that are issued to every user, with the old values withdrawn.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"控制網複測成果要以版本編號發布並記錄生效日期，所有放樣與監測系統須在同一天切換到新版坐標；參考點的選定與更換須經監測工程師與大地工程師共同核可。","textEn":"Issue re-surveyed control coordinates under a version number with an effective date, and switch every set-out and monitoring system to the new version on the same day; selection and replacement of reference points need joint approval of the monitoring engineer and the geotechnical engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網複測與移動判定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Network re-survey and movement testing\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","超高層核心筒在任何時刻都應該量測到完全垂直。","依施工進度訂定複測頻率（例如每月一次，重大開挖前後加測），以相同儀器與網形重測，做自由網或以已證實穩定的點平差，逐點做顯著性檢定。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A supertall core should measure perfectly vertical at any moment.","Set re-survey frequency by construction progress (for example monthly, with extra surveys before and after major excavation), re-observe with the same instruments and geometry, adjust as a free network or on proven-stable points, and test every point for significance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"依施工進度訂定複測頻率（例如每月一次，重大開挖前後加測），以相同儀器與網形重測，做自由網或以已證實穩定的點平差，逐點做顯著性檢定；判定移動的點要更新坐標並通知所有使用者，同時作廢舊坐標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Set re-survey frequency by construction progress (for example monthly, with extra surveys before and after major excavation), re-observe with the same instruments and geometry, adjust as a free network or on proven-stable points, and test every point for significance; points found to have moved get new coordinates that are issued to every user, with the old values withdrawn. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b097-v13-36","title":"控制網複測與移動判定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Network re-survey and movement testing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「參考點穩定性檢定」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reference-point stability test” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"監測站的參考稜鏡裝在會隨施工下沉的鄰近建物上，平差把參考點的沉陷平均分配到監測點，報表顯示軌道變位很小，實際沉陷卻被低估，警戒值觸發延遲。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reference prisms for a monitoring station are fixed to neighbouring buildings that settle with the works; the adjustment spreads the reference settlement over the monitored points, reports show small track movements, real settlement is underestimated and alarm triggers come late. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Crossrail 的自動化監測經驗也指出，參考稜鏡應設在影響範圍外並分散於各方向，平差不應過度修改原始觀測，以免掩蓋網形衰退。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Crossrail's automated monitoring experience likewise found that reference prisms should sit outside the zone of influence and be spread in many directions, and that adjustments should change raw observations as little as possible so that network decay is not hidden.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「監測點的變位一定代表結構移動，與參考點無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any movement of a monitored point means the structure moved, regardless of the reference points.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"監測站的參考稜鏡裝在會隨施工下沉的鄰近建物上，平差把參考點的沉陷平均分配到監測點，報表顯示軌道變位很小，實際沉陷卻被低估，警戒值觸發延遲。","textEn":"Reference prisms for a monitoring station are fixed to neighbouring buildings that settle with the works; the adjustment spreads the reference settlement over the monitored points, reports show small track movements, real settlement is underestimated and alarm triggers come late.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網複測與移動判定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Network re-survey and movement testing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["監測站的參考稜鏡裝在會隨施工下沉的鄰近建物上，平差把參考點的沉陷平均分配到監測點，報表顯示軌道變位很小，實際沉陷卻被低估，警戒值觸發延遲。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Reference prisms for a monitoring station are fixed to neighbouring buildings that settle with the works.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"監測站的參考稜鏡裝在會隨施工下沉的鄰近建物上，平差把參考點的沉陷平均分配到監測點，報表顯示軌道變位很小，實際沉陷卻被低估，警戒值觸發延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reference prisms for a monitoring station are fixed to neighbouring buildings that settle with the works; the adjustment spreads the reference settlement over the monitored points, reports show small track movements, real settlement is underestimated and alarm triggers come late. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b097-v13-37","title":"控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Control records, reference frames and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「點之記與參考框架」如何影響施工測量控制網的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Point records and reference frame” governs force, deformation or durability in “Construction surveying control networks”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"控制網的價值會延續到營運期：竣工測量、日後擴建、結構健康監測與災後檢查都需要找到原來的點與坐標。交接時若只留下坐標表，沒有點之記、坐標系統與參考框架版本、觀測日期與平差報告，日後的人無法判斷坐標是否仍可用。台灣這類板塊活動區的地殼每年都在移動，國家坐標框架也會更新版本，所以坐標必須連同參考框架與觀測時刻一起記錄。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「點之記與參考框架」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A control network's value lasts into operation: as-built surveys, later extensions, structural health monitoring and post-disaster inspections all need to find the original points and coordinates. If handover leaves only a coordinate list, without point descriptions, coordinate-system and reference-frame version, observation dates and adjustment reports, later users cannot judge whether the coordinates are still usable. In tectonically active regions such as Taiwan the crust moves every year and national frames are revised, so coordinates must be recorded together with their reference frame and epoch. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Point records and reference frame” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：兩個相距 20 km 的控制點，若相對地殼運動速率為每年 10 mm，5 年後相對位置差 10×5 = 50 mm，相當於 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm 的比例差；對 500 m 的結構約為 500×2.5×10⁻⁶ = 1.25 mm，對 20 km 的線形工程則會影響各段接軌。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Two control points 20 km apart with a relative crustal velocity of 10 mm per year drift 10×5 = 50 mm apart in 5 years, a scale discrepancy of 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm; for a 500 m structure that is about 500×2.5×10⁻⁶ = 1.25 mm, but across a 20 km linear work it affects how sections join.","failure":"常見誤解：「坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「點之記與參考框架」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Point records and reference frame”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-37-k1","title":"控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接","titleEn":"Control records, reference frames and handover","text":"控制網的價值會延續到營運期：竣工測量、日後擴建、結構健康監測與災後檢查都需要找到原來的點與坐標。交接時若只留下坐標表，沒有點之記、坐標系統與參考框架版本、觀測日期與平差報告，日後的人無法判斷坐標是否仍可用。","textEn":"A control network's value lasts into operation: as-built surveys, later extensions, structural health monitoring and post-disaster inspections all need to find the original points and coordinates. If handover leaves only a coordinate list, without point descriptions, coordinate-system and reference-frame version, observation dates and adjustment reports, later users cannot judge whether the coordinates are still usable.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control records, reference frames and handover\" is correct?","options":["坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。","控制網的價值會延續到營運期：竣工測量、日後擴建、結構健康監測與災後檢查都需要找到原來的點與坐標。","只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。"],"optionsEn":["Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough.","A control network's value lasts into operation: as-built surveys, later extensions, structural health monitoring and post-disaster inspections all need to find the original points and coordinates.","With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"控制網的價值會延續到營運期：竣工測量、日後擴建、結構健康監測與災後檢查都需要找到原來的點與坐標。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A control network's value lasts into operation: as-built surveys, later extensions, structural health monitoring and post-disaster inspections all need to find the original points and coordinates. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b097-v13-38","title":"控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Control records, reference frames and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「點之記與參考框架」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Point records and reference frame” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：兩個相距 20 km 的控制點，若相對地殼運動速率為每年 10 mm，5 年後相對位置差 10×5 = 50 mm，相當於 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm 的比例差；對 500 m 的結構約為 500×2.5×10⁻⁶ = 1.25 mm，對 20 km 的線形工程則會影響各段接軌。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Two control points 20 km apart with a relative crustal velocity of 10 mm per year drift 10×5 = 50 mm apart in 5 years, a scale discrepancy of 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm; for a 500 m structure that is about 500×2.5×10⁻⁶ = 1.25 mm, but across a 20 km linear work it affects how sections join. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交接前抽查控制點是否仍存在且未受損，重測部分點並與最新成果比較；交接文件清單應包含點之記、照片、坐標與高程表、參考框架與觀測時刻、平差報告及儀器校正證書，並由業主的資產管理單位確認可讀取。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before handover, spot-check that control points still exist undamaged, re-measure some and compare with the latest results; the handover list should include point descriptions, photographs, coordinate and height tables, reference frame and epoch, adjustment reports and instrument calibration certificates, confirmed as readable by the owner's asset-management team.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"兩個相距 20 km 的控制點，若相對地殼運動速率為每年 10 mm，5 年後相對位置差 10×5 = 50 mm，相當於 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm 的比例差；對 500 m 的結構約為 500×2.5×10⁻⁶ = 1.25 mm，對 20 km 的線形工程則會影響各段接軌。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Two control points 20 km apart with a relative crustal velocity of 10 mm per year drift 10×5 = 50 mm apart in 5 years, a scale discrepancy of 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm; for a 500 m structure that is about 500×2.5×10⁻⁶ = 1.25 mm, but across a 20 km linear work it affects how sections join. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control records, reference frames and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["控制點一旦埋設完成，坐標就永遠不會改變。","閉合差很小，就證明導線中沒有任何錯誤。","兩個相距 20 km 的控制點，若相對地殼運動速率為每年 10 mm，5 年後相對位置差 10×5 = 50 mm，相當於 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm 的比例差。"],"optionsEn":["Once a control point is installed, its coordinates never change.","A small misclosure proves the traverse contains no errors.","Two control points 20 km apart with a relative crustal velocity of 10 mm per year drift 10×5 = 50 mm apart in 5 years, a scale discrepancy of 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩個相距 20 km 的控制點，若相對地殼運動速率為每年 10 mm，5 年後相對位置差 10×5 = 50 mm，相當於 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm 的比例差；對 500 m 的結構約為 500×2.5×10⁻⁶ = 1.25 mm，對 20 km 的線形工程則會影響各段接軌。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Two control points 20 km apart with a relative crustal velocity of 10 mm per year drift 10×5 = 50 mm apart in 5 years, a scale discrepancy of 50 mm/20 km = 2.5 ppm; for a 500 m structure that is about 500×2.5×10⁻⁶ = 1.25 mm, but across a 20 km linear work it affects how sections join. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b097-v13-39","title":"控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control records, reference frames and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「點之記與參考框架」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Point records and reference frame” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交接前抽查控制點是否仍存在且未受損，重測部分點並與最新成果比較；交接文件清單應包含點之記、照片、坐標與高程表、參考框架與觀測時刻、平差報告及儀器校正證書，並由業主的資產管理單位確認可讀取。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before handover, spot-check that control points still exist undamaged, re-measure some and compare with the latest results; the handover list should include point descriptions, photographs, coordinate and height tables, reference frame and epoch, adjustment reports and instrument calibration certificates, confirmed as readable by the owner's asset-management team. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把需長期保留的控制點納入維護管理計畫，定期巡查與保護；所有坐標成果一律註明坐標系統、參考框架、高程基準與觀測時刻，交接文件由業主的測量代表簽收。","observationEn":"Site practice: Include long-term control points in the maintenance plan with periodic inspection and protection; label every coordinate result with coordinate system, reference frame, height datum and epoch, and have the owner's survey representative sign for the handover documents.","failure":"注意干擾：竣工多年後要做補強或擴建，原控制點已被鋪面覆蓋，坐標表也沒有註明參考框架版本，新團隊以新版國家坐標重新放樣，與既有結構差了數公分，接合構件無法安裝。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Years after completion a strengthening or extension project finds the original control points paved over and the coordinate list silent on the reference-frame version; the new team sets out in the revised national frame, misses the existing structure by several centimetres, and connecting members cannot be installed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交接前抽查控制點是否仍存在且未受損，重測部分點並與最新成果比較；交接文件清單應包含點之記、照片、坐標與高程表、參考框架與觀測時刻、平差報告及儀器校正證書，並由業主的資產管理單位確認可讀取。","textEn":"Before handover, spot-check that control points still exist undamaged, re-measure some and compare with the latest results; the handover list should include point descriptions, photographs, coordinate and height tables, reference frame and epoch, adjustment reports and instrument calibration certificates, confirmed as readable by the owner's asset-management team.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把需長期保留的控制點納入維護管理計畫，定期巡查與保護；所有坐標成果一律註明坐標系統、參考框架、高程基準與觀測時刻，交接文件由業主的測量代表簽收。","textEn":"Include long-term control points in the maintenance plan with periodic inspection and protection; label every coordinate result with coordinate system, reference frame, height datum and epoch, and have the owner's survey representative sign for the handover documents.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control records, reference frames and handover\"?","options":["交接前抽查控制點是否仍存在且未受損，重測部分點並與最新成果比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","GNSS 量到的高程就是海拔高度。"],"optionsEn":["Before handover, spot-check that control points still exist undamaged, re-measure some and compare with the latest results.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The height measured by GNSS is the height above sea level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交接前抽查控制點是否仍存在且未受損，重測部分點並與最新成果比較；交接文件清單應包含點之記、照片、坐標與高程表、參考框架與觀測時刻、平差報告及儀器校正證書，並由業主的資產管理單位確認可讀取。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before handover, spot-check that control points still exist undamaged, re-measure some and compare with the latest results; the handover list should include point descriptions, photographs, coordinate and height tables, reference frame and epoch, adjustment reports and instrument calibration certificates, confirmed as readable by the owner's asset-management team. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b097-v13-40","title":"控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control records, reference frames and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b097-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「點之記與參考框架」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Point records and reference frame” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"竣工多年後要做補強或擴建，原控制點已被鋪面覆蓋，坐標表也沒有註明參考框架版本，新團隊以新版國家坐標重新放樣，與既有結構差了數公分，接合構件無法安裝。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Years after completion a strengthening or extension project finds the original control points paved over and the coordinate list silent on the reference-frame version; the new team sets out in the revised national frame, misses the existing structure by several centimetres, and connecting members cannot be installed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：台灣這類板塊活動區的地殼每年都在移動，國家坐標框架也會更新版本，所以坐標必須連同參考框架與觀測時刻一起記錄。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In tectonically active regions such as Taiwan the crust moves every year and national frames are revised, so coordinates must be recorded together with their reference frame and epoch.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「坐標是永久不變的數字，只要記錄數值本身就足夠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Coordinates are permanent numbers, so recording the values alone is enough.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b097-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"竣工多年後要做補強或擴建，原控制點已被鋪面覆蓋，坐標表也沒有註明參考框架版本，新團隊以新版國家坐標重新放樣，與既有結構差了數公分，接合構件無法安裝。","textEn":"Years after completion a strengthening or extension project finds the original control points paved over and the coordinate list silent on the reference-frame version; the new team sets out in the revised national frame, misses the existing structure by several centimetres, and connecting members cannot be installed.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]},{"id":"b097-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制成果紀錄、參考框架與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control records, reference frames and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","竣工多年後要做補強或擴建，原控制點已被鋪面覆蓋，坐標表也沒有註明參考框架版本，新團隊以新版國家坐標重新放樣，與既有結構差了數公分，接合構件無法安裝。","只要用最精密的儀器，就不需要規劃控制網層級與誤差分配。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Years after completion a strengthening or extension project finds the original control points paved over and the coordinate list silent on the reference-frame version.","With the most precise instrument there is no need to plan network hierarchy or error allocation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"竣工多年後要做補強或擴建，原控制點已被鋪面覆蓋，坐標表也沒有註明參考框架版本，新團隊以新版國家坐標重新放樣，與既有結構差了數公分，接合構件無法安裝。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Years after completion a strengthening or extension project finds the original control points paved over and the coordinate list silent on the reference-frame version; the new team sets out in the revised national frame, misses the existing structure by several centimetres, and connecting members cannot be installed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-ats-monitoring","v13s-iso-17123-5","v13s-noaa-ngs-58","v13s-wiki-gotthard-de","v13s-wiki-channel-tunnel"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
